{"surah": 26, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "طسٓمٓ ", "translation": "Ṭā, Seen, Meem.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "طسٓمٓ", "translit": "ٓmٓsṭ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "تِلْكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ ٱلْمُبِينِ ", "translation": "These are the verses of the clear Book.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تِلْكَ", "translit": "َkْlِt", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَايَٰتُ", "translit": "ُtَٰyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْكِتَٰبِ", "translit": "ِbَٰtِkْlٱ", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُبِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِbُmْlٱ", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "لَعَلَّكَ بَٰخِعٌ نَّفْسَكَ أَلَّا يَكُونُوا۟ مُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Perhaps, [O Muḥammad], you would kill yourself with grief that they will not be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَعَلَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَٰخِعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعِhkَٰb", "root": "بخع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَّفْسَكَ", "translit": "َkَsْfَّn", "root": "نفس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَكُونُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnwُkَy", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "إِن نَّشَأْ نُنَزِّلْ عَلَيْهِم مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ ءَايَةً فَظَلَّتْ أَعْنَٰقُهُمْ لَهَا خَٰضِعِينَ ", "translation": "If We willed, We could send down to them from the sky a sign for which their necks would remain humbled.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَّشَأْ", "translit": "ْaʾَhsَّn", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُنَزِّلْ", "translit": "ْlِّzَnُn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَظَلَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّlَẓَf", "root": "ظلل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَعْنَٰقُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُqَٰnْʿعَaʾ", "root": "عنق"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "لَهَا", "translit": "āَhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "خَٰضِعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعِḍَٰhk", "root": "خضع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَمَا يَأْتِيهِم مِّن ذِكْرٍ مِّنَ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ مُحْدَثٍ إِلَّا كَانُوا۟ عَنْهُ مُعْرِضِينَ ", "translation": "And no mention [i.e., revelation] comes to them anew from the Most Merciful except that they turn away from it.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَأْتِيهِم", "translit": "mِhyِtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ذِكْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ", "translit": "ِnَٰmْḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُحْدَثٍ", "translit": "ٍhtَdْḥُm", "root": "حدث"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَنْهُ", "translit": "ُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "مُعْرِضِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḍِrْʿعُm", "root": "عرض"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "فَقَدْ كَذَّبُوا۟ فَسَيَأْتِيهِمْ أَنۢبَٰٓؤُا۟ مَا كَانُوا۟ بِهِۦ يَسْتَهْزِءُونَ ", "translation": "For they have already denied, but there will come to them the news of that which they used to ridicule.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَذَّبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَسَيَأْتِيهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhyِtْaʾَyَsَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنۢبَٰٓؤُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwʾَٰٓbۢnَaʾ", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَسْتَهْزِءُونَ", "translit": "َnwُءِzْhَtْsَy", "root": "هزا"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "أَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ إِلَى ٱلْأَرْضِ كَمْ أَنۢبَتْنَا فِيهَا مِن كُلِّ زَوْجٍ كَرِيمٍ ", "translation": "Did they not look at the earth - how much We have produced therein from every noble kind?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَرَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَى", "translit": "àَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَمْ", "translit": "ْmَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَنۢبَتْنَا", "translit": "āَnْtَbۢnَaʾ", "root": "نبت"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "زَوْجٍ", "translit": "ٍjgْwَz", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "كَرِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِrَk", "root": "كرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَإِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبُّكَ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنِ ٱئْتِ ٱلْقَوْمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "And [mention] when your Lord called Moses, [saying], \"Go to the wrongdoing people -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَادَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَdāَn", "root": "ندي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَنِ", "translit": "ِnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱئْتِ", "translit": "ِtْyʾٱ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْقَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَqْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَّٰẓlٱ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "قَوْمَ فِرْعَوْنَۚ أَلَا يَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "The people of Pharaoh. Will they not fear Allāh?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِرْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْrِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَy", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّىٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُكَذِّبُونِ ", "translation": "He said, \"My Lord, indeed I fear that they will deny me", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَخَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَhkَaʾ", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُكَذِّبُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُbِّhdَkُy", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "وَيَضِيقُ صَدْرِى وَلَا يَنطَلِقُ لِسَانِى فَأَرْسِلْ إِلَىٰ هَٰرُونَ ", "translation": "And that my breast will tighten and my tongue will not be fluent, so send for Aaron.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَضِيقُ", "translit": "ُqyِḍَyَw", "root": "ضيق"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَدْرِى", "translit": "àِrْdَṣ", "root": "صدر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَنطَلِقُ", "translit": "ُqِlَṭnَy", "root": "طلق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِسَانِى", "translit": "àِnāَsِl", "root": "لسن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَأَرْسِلْ", "translit": "ْlِsْrَaʾَf", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "هَٰرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَٰh", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "وَلَهُمْ عَلَىَّ ذَنۢبٌ فَأَخَافُ أَن يَقْتُلُونِ ", "translation": "And they have upon me a [claim due to] sin, so I fear that they will kill me.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَنۢبٌ", "translit": "ٌbۢnَhd", "root": "ذنب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَأَخَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَhkَaʾَf", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَقْتُلُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُlُtْqَy", "root": "قتل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "قَالَ كَلَّاۖ فَٱذْهَبَا بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآۖ إِنَّا مَعَكُم مُّسْتَمِعُونَ ", "translation": "[Allāh] said, \"No. Go both of you with Our signs; indeed, We are with you, listening.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَلَّا", "translit": "āَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَٱذْهَبَا", "translit": "āَbَhْhdٱَf", "root": "ذهب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnِtَٰyāَٔـِb", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَعَكُم", "translit": "mُkَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُّسْتَمِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِmَtْsُّm", "root": "سمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "فَأْتِيَا فِرْعَوْنَ فَقُولَآ إِنَّا رَسُولُ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "Go to Pharaoh and say, 'We are the messengers[1] of the Lord of the worlds,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأْتِيَا", "translit": "āَyِtْaʾَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِرْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْrِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَقُولَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlwُqَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَسُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "أَنْ أَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ", "translation": "[Commanded to say], \"Send with us the Children of Israel.\"'\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْسِلْ", "translit": "ْlِsْrَaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَعَنَا", "translit": "āَnَʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَb", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِءَٰٓrْsِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "قَالَ أَلَمْ نُرَبِّكَ فِينَا وَلِيدًا وَلَبِثْتَ فِينَا مِنْ عُمُرِكَ سِنِينَ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said, \"Did we not raise you among us as a child, and you remained among us for years of your life?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُرَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَrُn", "root": "ربو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِينَا", "translit": "āَnyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلِيدًا", "translit": "āًdyِlَw", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَبِثْتَ", "translit": "َtْhtِbَlَw", "root": "لبث"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِينَا", "translit": "āَnyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عُمُرِكَ", "translit": "َkِrُmُʿع", "root": "عمر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "سِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِs", "root": "سنو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَفَعَلْتَ فَعْلَتَكَ ٱلَّتِى فَعَلْتَ وَأَنتَ مِنَ ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ ", "translation": "And [then] you did your deed which you did,[1] and you were of the ungrateful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَفَعَلْتَ", "translit": "َtْlَʿعَfَw", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَعْلَتَكَ", "translit": "َkَtَlْʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلَّتِى", "translit": "àِtَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَعَلْتَ", "translit": "َtْlَʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَأَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِfَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كفر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "قَالَ فَعَلْتُهَآ إِذًا وَأَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلضَّآلِّينَ ", "translation": "[Moses] said, \"I did it, then, while I was of those astray [i.e., ignorant].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَعَلْتُهَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhُtْlَʿعَf", "root": "فعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِذًا", "translit": "āًhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَأَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلضَّآلِّينَ", "translit": "َnyِّlٓāَّḍlٱ", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "فَفَرَرْتُ مِنكُمْ لَمَّا خِفْتُكُمْ فَوَهَبَ لِى رَبِّى حُكْمًا وَجَعَلَنِى مِنَ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "So I fled from you when I feared you. Then my Lord granted me judgement [i.e., wisdom and prophethood] and appointed me [as one] of the messengers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَفَرَرْتُ", "translit": "ُtْrَrَfَf", "root": "فرر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُknِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خِفْتُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُtْfِhk", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَوَهَبَ", "translit": "َbَhَwَf", "root": "وهب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "حُكْمًا", "translit": "āًmْkُḥ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَجَعَلَنِى", "translit": "àِnَlَʿعَjgَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "وَتِلْكَ نِعْمَةٌ تَمُنُّهَا عَلَىَّ أَنْ عَبَّدتَّ بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ", "translation": "And is this a favor of which you remind me - that you have enslaved the Children of Israel?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتِلْكَ", "translit": "َkْlِtَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نِعْمَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَmْʿعِn", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "تَمُنُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّnُmَt", "root": "منن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَبَّدتَّ", "translit": "َّtdَّbَʿع", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَb", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِءَٰٓrْsِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "قَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "Said Pharaoh, \"And what is the Lord of the worlds?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِرْعَوْنُ", "translit": "ُnْwَʿعْrِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "رَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "قَالَ رَبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَآۖ إِن كُنتُم مُّوقِنِينَ ", "translation": "[Moses] said, \"The Lord of the heavens and earth and that between them, if you should be convinced.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰwَٰmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱَw", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُنتُم", "translit": "mُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُّوقِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِqwُّm", "root": "يقن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "قَالَ لِمَنْ حَوْلَهُۥٓ أَلَا تَسْتَمِعُونَ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said to those around him, \"Do you not hear?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِمَنْ", "translit": "ْnَmِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَوْلَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَlْwَḥ", "root": "حول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَسْتَمِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِmَtْsَt", "root": "سمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 26, "text": "قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ ءَابَآئِكُمُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "[Moses] said, \"Your Lord and the Lord of your first forefathers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبُّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَرَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَrَw", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَابَآئِكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkِyʾٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 27, "text": "قَالَ إِنَّ رَسُولَكُمُ ٱلَّذِىٓ أُرْسِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ لَمَجْنُونٌ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said,[1] \"Indeed, your 'messenger' who has been sent to you is mad.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَسُولَكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkَlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أُرْسِلَ", "translit": "َlِsْrُaʾ", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَمَجْنُونٌ", "translit": "ٌnwُnْjgَmَl", "root": "جنن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 28, "text": "قَالَ رَبُّ ٱلْمَشْرِقِ وَٱلْمَغْرِبِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَآۖ إِن كُنتُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ ", "translation": "[Moses] said, \"Lord of the east and the west and that between them, if you were to reason.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبُّ", "translit": "ُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمَشْرِقِ", "translit": "ِqِrْhsَmْlٱ", "root": "شرق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلْمَغْرِبِ", "translit": "ِbِrْغَmْlٱَw", "root": "غرب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَيْنَهُمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmُhَnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "تَعْقِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِqْʿعَt", "root": "عقل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 29, "text": "قَالَ لَئِنِ ٱتَّخَذْتَ إِلَٰهًا غَيْرِى لَأَجْعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلْمَسْجُونِينَ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said, \"If you take a god other than me, I will surely place you among those imprisoned.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَئِنِ", "translit": "ِnِyʾَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱتَّخَذْتَ", "translit": "َtْhdَhkَّtٱ", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَٰهًا", "translit": "āًhَٰlِiʾ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "غَيْرِى", "translit": "àِrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَأَجْعَلَنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnَlَʿعْjgَaʾَl", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْمَسْجُونِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnwُjgْsَmْlٱ", "root": "سجن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 30, "text": "قَالَ أَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكَ بِشَىْءٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "[Moses] said, \"Even if I brought you something [i.e., proof] manifest?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَوَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جِئْتُكَ", "translit": "َkُtْyʾِjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِشَىْءٍ", "translit": "ٍءْàَhsِb", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 31, "text": "قَالَ فَأْتِ بِهِۦٓ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said, \"Then bring it, if you should be of the truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَأْتِ", "translit": "ِtْaʾَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِۦٓ", "translit": "ٓۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُنتَ", "translit": "َtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 32, "text": "فَأَلْقَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "So [Moses] threw his staff, and suddenly it was a serpent manifest.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَلْقَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَqْlَaʾَf", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَصَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَṣَʿع", "root": "عصو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ثُعْبَانٌ", "translit": "ٌnāَbْʿعُht", "root": "ثعب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 33, "text": "وَنَزَعَ يَدَهُۥ فَإِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنَّٰظِرِينَ ", "translation": "And he drew out his hand; thereupon it was white for the observers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَنَزَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَzَnَw", "root": "نزع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَدَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَdَy", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَيْضَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَḍْyَb", "root": "بيض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لِلنَّٰظِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِẓَّٰnlِl", "root": "نظر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 34, "text": "قَالَ لِلْمَلَإِ حَوْلَهُۥٓ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَسَٰحِرٌ عَلِيمٌ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said to the eminent ones around him, \"Indeed, this is a learned magician.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلْمَلَإِ", "translit": "ِiʾَlَmْlِl", "root": "ملا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَوْلَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَlْwَḥ", "root": "حول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "هَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَسَٰحِرٌ", "translit": "ٌrِḥَٰsَl", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 35, "text": "يُرِيدُ أَن يُخْرِجَكُم مِّنْ أَرْضِكُم بِسِحْرِهِۦ فَمَاذَا تَأْمُرُونَ ", "translation": "He wants to drive you out of your land by his magic, so what do you advise?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يُرِيدُ", "translit": "ُdyِrُy", "root": "رود"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُخْرِجَكُم", "translit": "mُkَjgِrْhkُy", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَرْضِكُم", "translit": "mُkِḍْrَaʾ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِسِحْرِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِrْḥِsِb", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَمَاذَا", "translit": "āَhdāَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "تَأْمُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُmْaʾَt", "root": "امر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 36, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ أَرْجِهْ وَأَخَاهُ وَٱبْعَثْ فِى ٱلْمَدَآئِنِ حَٰشِرِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"Postpone [the matter of] him and his brother and send among the cities gatherers", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَرْجِهْ", "translit": "ْhِjgْrَaʾ", "root": "رجو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَخَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَhkَaʾَw", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱبْعَثْ", "translit": "ْhtَʿعْbٱَw", "root": "بعث"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمَدَآئِنِ", "translit": "ِnِyʾٓāَdَmْlٱ", "root": "مدن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "حَٰشِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhsَٰḥ", "root": "حشر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 37, "text": "يَأْتُوكَ بِكُلِّ سَحَّارٍ عَلِيمٍ ", "translation": "Who will bring you every learned, skilled magician.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَأْتُوكَ", "translit": "َkwُtْaʾَy", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِb", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَحَّارٍ", "translit": "ٍrāَّḥَs", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِlَʿع", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 38, "text": "فَجُمِعَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ لِمِيقَٰتِ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ ", "translation": "So the magicians were assembled for the appointment of a well-known day.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَجُمِعَ", "translit": "َʿعِmُjgَf", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّحَرَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَrَḥَّslٱ", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِمِيقَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰqyِmِl", "root": "وقت"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَّعْلُومٍ", "translit": "ٍmwُlْʿعَّm", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 39, "text": "وَقِيلَ لِلنَّاسِ هَلْ أَنتُم مُّجْتَمِعُونَ ", "translation": "And it was said to the people, \"Will you congregate", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلنَّاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَّnlِl", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنتُم", "translit": "mُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُّجْتَمِعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعِmَtْjgُّm", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 40, "text": "لَعَلَّنَا نَتَّبِعُ ٱلسَّحَرَةَ إِن كَانُوا۟ هُمُ ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ ", "translation": "That we might follow the magicians if they are the predominant?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَعَلَّنَا", "translit": "āَnَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَتَّبِعُ", "translit": "ُʿعِbَّtَn", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّحَرَةَ", "translit": "َẗَrَḥَّslٱ", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "هُمُ", "translit": "ُmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِlَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غلب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 41, "text": "فَلَمَّا جَآءَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ قَالُوا۟ لِفِرْعَوْنَ أَئِنَّ لَنَا لَأَجْرًا إِن كُنَّا نَحْنُ ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ ", "translation": "And when the magicians arrived, they said to Pharaoh, \"Is there indeed for us a reward if we are the predominant?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّحَرَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَrَḥَّslٱ", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِفِرْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْrِfِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَئِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِyʾَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَأَجْرًا", "translit": "āًrْjgَaʾَl", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰلِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِlَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غلب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 42, "text": "قَالَ نَعَمْ وَإِنَّكُمْ إِذًا لَّمِنَ ٱلْمُقَرَّبِينَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Yes, and indeed, you will then be of those near [to me].\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَعَمْ", "translit": "ْmَʿعَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَإِنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذًا", "translit": "āًhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَّمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُقَرَّبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَّrَqُmْlٱ", "root": "قرب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 43, "text": "قَالَ لَهُم مُّوسَىٰٓ أَلْقُوا۟ مَآ أَنتُم مُّلْقُونَ ", "translation": "Moses said to them, \"Throw whatever you will throw.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُم", "translit": "mُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُّوسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَswُّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَلْقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqْlَaʾ", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَنتُم", "translit": "mُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُّلْقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqْlُّm", "root": "لقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 44, "text": "فَأَلْقَوْا۟ حِبَالَهُمْ وَعِصِيَّهُمْ وَقَالُوا۟ بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّا لَنَحْنُ ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ ", "translation": "So they threw their ropes and their staffs and said, \"By the might of Pharaoh, indeed it is we who are predominant.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَلْقَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَqْlَaʾَf", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حِبَالَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَlāَbِḥ", "root": "حبل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَعِصِيَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّyِṣِʿعَw", "root": "عصو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَقَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِعِزَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّzِʿعِb", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فِرْعَوْنَ", "translit": "َnْwَʿعْrِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَنَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰلِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِlَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غلب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 45, "text": "فَأَلْقَىٰ مُوسَىٰ عَصَاهُ فَإِذَا هِىَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَأْفِكُونَ ", "translation": "Then Moses threw his staff, and at once it devoured what they falsified.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَلْقَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَqْlَaʾَf", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَصَاهُ", "translit": "ُhāَṣَʿع", "root": "عصو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَلْقَفُ", "translit": "ُfَqْlَt", "root": "لقف"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَأْفِكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkِfْaʾَy", "root": "افك"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 46, "text": "فَأُلْقِىَ ٱلسَّحَرَةُ سَٰجِدِينَ ", "translation": "So the magicians fell down in prostration [to Allāh].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأُلْقِىَ", "translit": "َàِqْlُaʾَf", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّحَرَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَrَḥَّslٱ", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "سَٰجِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِjgَٰs", "root": "سجد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 47, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ ءَامَنَّا بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"We have believed in the Lord of the worlds,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَامَنَّا", "translit": "āَّnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِرَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 48, "text": "رَبِّ مُوسَىٰ وَهَٰرُونَ ", "translation": "The Lord of Moses and Aaron.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَهَٰرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَٰhَw", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 49, "text": "قَالَ ءَامَنتُمْ لَهُۥ قَبْلَ أَنْ ءَاذَنَ لَكُمْۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَكَبِيرُكُمُ ٱلَّذِى عَلَّمَكُمُ ٱلسِّحْرَ فَلَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُونَۚ لَأُقَطِّعَنَّ أَيْدِيَكُمْ وَأَرْجُلَكُم مِّنْ خِلَٰفٍ وَلَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ ", "translation": "[Pharaoh] said, \"You believed him [i.e., Moses] before I gave you permission. Indeed, he is your leader who has taught you magic, but you are going to know. I will surely cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides, and I will surely crucify you all.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ءَامَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَبْلَ", "translit": "َlْbَq", "root": "قبل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ءَاذَنَ", "translit": "َnَhdāَء", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "لَكَبِيرُكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkُryِbَkَl", "root": "كبر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَلَّمَكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkَmَّlَʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "ٱلسِّحْرَ", "translit": "َrْḥِّslٱ", "root": "سحر"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "فَلَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "لَأُقَطِّعَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَʿعِّṭَqُaʾَl", "root": "قطع"}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "أَيْدِيَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَyِdْyَaʾ", "root": "يدي"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "وَأَرْجُلَكُم", "translit": "mُkَlُjgْrَaʾَw", "root": "رجل"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "خِلَٰفٍ", "translit": "ٍfَٰlِhk", "root": "خلف"}, {"id": 20, "arabic": "وَلَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّnَbِّlَṣُaʾَlَw", "root": "صلب"}, {"id": 21, "arabic": "أَجْمَعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 50, "text": "قَالُوا۟ لَا ضَيْرَۖ إِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا مُنقَلِبُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"No harm. Indeed, to our Lord we will return.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ضَيْرَ", "translit": "َrْyَḍ", "root": "ضير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبِّنَا", "translit": "āَnِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُنقَلِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِlَqnُm", "root": "قلب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 51, "text": "إِنَّا نَطْمَعُ أَن يَغْفِرَ لَنَا رَبُّنَا خَطَٰيَٰنَآ أَن كُنَّآ أَوَّلَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, we aspire that our Lord will forgive us our sins because we were the first of the believers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَطْمَعُ", "translit": "ُʿعَmْṭَn", "root": "طمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَغْفِرَ", "translit": "َrِfْغَy", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبُّنَا", "translit": "āَnُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "خَطَٰيَٰنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَٰyَٰṭَhk", "root": "خطا"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كُنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "أَوَّلَ", "translit": "َlَّwَaʾ", "root": "اول"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 52, "text": "وَأَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنْ أَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىٓ إِنَّكُم مُّتَّبَعُونَ ", "translation": "And We inspired to Moses, \"Travel by night with My servants; indeed, you will be pursued.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَوْحَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَḥْwَaʾَw", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنْ", "translit": "ْnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَسْرِ", "translit": "ِrْsَaʾ", "root": "سري"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِعِبَادِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِdāَbِʿعِb", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّتَّبَعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَbَّtُّm", "root": "تبع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 53, "text": "فَأَرْسَلَ فِرْعَوْنُ فِى ٱلْمَدَآئِنِ حَٰشِرِينَ ", "translation": "Then Pharaoh sent among the cities gatherers[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَرْسَلَ", "translit": "َlَsْrَaʾَf", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِرْعَوْنُ", "translit": "ُnْwَʿعْrِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمَدَآئِنِ", "translit": "ِnِyʾٓāَdَmْlٱ", "root": "مدن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "حَٰشِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhsَٰḥ", "root": "حشر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 54, "text": "إِنَّ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ لَشِرْذِمَةٌ قَلِيلُونَ ", "translation": "[And said], \"Indeed, those are but a small band,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَlُwʾَٰٓh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَشِرْذِمَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَmِhdْrِhsَl", "root": "شرذم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَلِيلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlyِlَq", "root": "قلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 55, "text": "وَإِنَّهُمْ لَنَا لَغَآئِظُونَ ", "translation": "And indeed, they are enraging us,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَغَآئِظُونَ", "translit": "َnwُẓِyʾٓāَغَl", "root": "غيظ"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 56, "text": "وَإِنَّا لَجَمِيعٌ حَٰذِرُونَ ", "translation": "And indeed, we are a cautious society...\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَجَمِيعٌ", "translit": "ٌʿعyِmَjgَl", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَٰذِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِhdَٰḥ", "root": "حذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 57, "text": "فَأَخْرَجْنَٰهُم مِّن جَنَّٰتٍ وَعُيُونٍ ", "translation": "So We removed them from gardens and springs", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَخْرَجْنَٰهُم", "translit": "mُhَٰnْjgَrْhkَaʾَf", "root": "خرج"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعُيُونٍ", "translit": "ٍnwُyُʿعَw", "root": "عين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 58, "text": "وَكُنُوزٍ وَمَقَامٍ كَرِيمٍ ", "translation": "And treasures and honorable station[1] -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَكُنُوزٍ", "translit": "ٍzwُnُkَw", "root": "كنز"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَقَامٍ", "translit": "ٍmāَqَmَw", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَرِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِrَk", "root": "كرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 59, "text": "كَذَٰلِكَ وَأَوْرَثْنَٰهَا بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ", "translation": "Thus. And We caused to inherit it the Children of Israel.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَأَوْرَثْنَٰهَا", "translit": "āَhَٰnْhtَrْwَaʾَw", "root": "ورث"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَb", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِءَٰٓrْsِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 60, "text": "فَأَتْبَعُوهُم مُّشْرِقِينَ ", "translation": "So they pursued them at sunrise.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَتْبَعُوهُم", "translit": "mُhwُʿعَbْtَaʾَf", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مُّشْرِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِrْhsُّm", "root": "شرق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 61, "text": "فَلَمَّا تَرَٰٓءَا ٱلْجَمْعَانِ قَالَ أَصْحَٰبُ مُوسَىٰٓ إِنَّا لَمُدْرَكُونَ ", "translation": "And when the two companies saw one another, the companions of Moses said, \"Indeed, we are to be overtaken!\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَرَٰٓءَا", "translit": "āَءَٰٓrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْجَمْعَانِ", "translit": "ِnāَʿعْmَjgْlٱ", "root": "جمع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "إِنَّا", "translit": "āَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَمُدْرَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَrْdُmَl", "root": "درك"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 62, "text": "قَالَ كَلَّآۖ إِنَّ مَعِىَ رَبِّى سَيَهْدِينِ ", "translation": "[Moses] said, \"No! Indeed, with me is my Lord; He will guide me.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَلَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّlَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَعِىَ", "translit": "َàِʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَيَهْدِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِdْhَyَs", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 63, "text": "فَأَوْحَيْنَآ إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰٓ أَنِ ٱضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ ٱلْبَحْرَۖ فَٱنفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَٱلطَّوْدِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ ", "translation": "Then We inspired to Moses, \"Strike with your staff the sea,\" and it parted, and each portion was like a great towering mountain.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَوْحَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَḥْwَaʾَf", "root": "وحي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَنِ", "translit": "ِnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱضْرِب", "translit": "bِrْḍٱ", "root": "ضرب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِّعَصَاكَ", "translit": "َkāَṣَʿعِّb", "root": "عصو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْبَحْرَ", "translit": "َrْḥَbْlٱ", "root": "بحر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَٱنفَلَقَ", "translit": "َqَlَfnٱَf", "root": "فلق"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "فَكَانَ", "translit": "َnāَkَf", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "كُلُّ", "translit": "ُّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "فِرْقٍ", "translit": "ٍqْrِf", "root": "فرق"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "كَٱلطَّوْدِ", "translit": "ِdْwَّṭlٱَk", "root": "طود"}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ٱلْعَظِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِẓَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 64, "text": "وَأَزْلَفْنَا ثَمَّ ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ ", "translation": "And We advanced thereto the others [i.e., the pursuers].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَزْلَفْنَا", "translit": "āَnْfَlْzَaʾَw", "root": "زلف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ثَمَّ", "translit": "َّmَht", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 65, "text": "وَأَنجَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ وَمَن مَّعَهُۥٓ أَجْمَعِينَ ", "translation": "And We saved Moses and those with him, all together.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنجَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَjgnَaʾَw", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مُوسَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَswُm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّعَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَʿعَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْمَعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 66, "text": "ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ ", "translation": "Then We drowned the others.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَغْرَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَrْغَaʾ", "root": "غرق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 67, "text": "إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 68, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 69, "text": "وَٱتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ ", "translation": "And recite to them the news of Abraham,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱتْلُ", "translit": "ُlْtٱَw", "root": "تلو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَبَأَ", "translit": "َaʾَbَn", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِبْرَٰهِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِhَٰrْbِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 70, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لِأَبِيهِ وَقَوْمِهِۦ مَا تَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "When he said to his father and his people, \"What do you worship?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِأَبِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِbَaʾِl", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَقَوْمِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِmْwَqَw", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 71, "text": "قَالُوا۟ نَعْبُدُ أَصْنَامًا فَنَظَلُّ لَهَا عَٰكِفِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"We worship idols and remain to them devoted.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَعْبُدُ", "translit": "ُdُbْʿعَn", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَصْنَامًا", "translit": "āًmāَnْṣَaʾ", "root": "صنم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَنَظَلُّ", "translit": "ُّlَẓَnَf", "root": "ظلل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَهَا", "translit": "āَhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَٰكِفِينَ", "translit": "َnyِfِkَٰʿع", "root": "عكف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 72, "text": "قَالَ هَلْ يَسْمَعُونَكُمْ إِذْ تَدْعُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Do they hear you when you supplicate?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَسْمَعُونَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnwُʿعَmْsَy", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَدْعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعْdَt", "root": "دعو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 73, "text": "أَوْ يَنفَعُونَكُمْ أَوْ يَضُرُّونَ ", "translation": "Or do they benefit you, or do they harm?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنفَعُونَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnwُʿعَfnَy", "root": "نفع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَضُرُّونَ", "translit": "َnwُّrُḍَy", "root": "ضرر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 74, "text": "قَالُوا۟ بَلْ وَجَدْنَآ ءَابَآءَنَا كَذَٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"But we found our fathers doing thus.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَجَدْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْdَjgَw", "root": "وجد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَابَآءَنَا", "translit": "āَnَءٓāَbāَء", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَفْعَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَʿعْfَy", "root": "فعل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 75, "text": "قَالَ أَفَرَءَيْتُم مَّا كُنتُمْ تَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Then do you see what you have been worshipping,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَفَرَءَيْتُم", "translit": "mُtْyَءَrَfَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 76, "text": "أَنتُمْ وَءَابَآؤُكُمُ ٱلْأَقْدَمُونَ ", "translation": "You and your ancient forefathers?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَءَابَآؤُكُمُ", "translit": "ُmُkُwʾٓāَbāَءَw", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْأَقْدَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَdْqَaʾْlٱ", "root": "قدم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 77, "text": "فَإِنَّهُمْ عَدُوٌّ لِّىٓ إِلَّا رَبَّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed, they are enemies to me, except the Lord of the worlds,[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَدُوٌّ", "translit": "ٌّwُdَʿع", "root": "عدو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبَّ", "translit": "َّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 78, "text": "ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَنِى فَهُوَ يَهْدِينِ ", "translation": "Who created me, and He [it is who] guides me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقَنِى", "translit": "àِnَqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَهْدِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِdْhَy", "root": "هدي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 79, "text": "وَٱلَّذِى هُوَ يُطْعِمُنِى وَيَسْقِينِ ", "translation": "And it is He who feeds me and gives me drink.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُطْعِمُنِى", "translit": "àِnُmِʿعْṭُy", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَيَسْقِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِqْsَyَw", "root": "سقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 80, "text": "وَإِذَا مَرِضْتُ فَهُوَ يَشْفِينِ ", "translation": "And when I am ill, it is He who cures me", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَرِضْتُ", "translit": "ُtْḍِrَm", "root": "مرض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَشْفِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِfْhsَy", "root": "شفي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 81, "text": "وَٱلَّذِى يُمِيتُنِى ثُمَّ يُحْيِينِ ", "translation": "And who will cause me to die and then bring me to life", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُمِيتُنِى", "translit": "àِnُtyِmُy", "root": "موت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُحْيِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِyْḥُy", "root": "حيي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 82, "text": "وَٱلَّذِىٓ أَطْمَعُ أَن يَغْفِرَ لِى خَطِيٓـَٔتِى يَوْمَ ٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "And who I aspire that He will forgive me my sin on the Day of Recompense.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَطْمَعُ", "translit": "ُʿعَmْṭَaʾ", "root": "طمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَغْفِرَ", "translit": "َrِfْغَy", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "خَطِيٓـَٔتِى", "translit": "àِtَٔـٓyِṭَhk", "root": "خطا"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 83, "text": "رَبِّ هَبْ لِى حُكْمًا وَأَلْحِقْنِى بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ", "translation": "[And he said], \"My Lord, grant me authority and join me with the righteous.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَبْ", "translit": "ْbَh", "root": "وهب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِى", "translit": "àِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حُكْمًا", "translit": "āًmْkُḥ", "root": "حكم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَأَلْحِقْنِى", "translit": "àِnْqِḥْlَaʾَw", "root": "لحق"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥِlَّٰṣlٱِb", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 84, "text": "وَٱجْعَل لِّى لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ ", "translation": "And grant me a mention [i.e., reputation] of honor among later generations.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱجْعَل", "translit": "lَʿعْjgٱَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِّى", "translit": "àِّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِسَانَ", "translit": "َnāَsِl", "root": "لسن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "صِدْقٍ", "translit": "ٍqْdِṣ", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 85, "text": "وَٱجْعَلْنِى مِن وَرَثَةِ جَنَّةِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ", "translation": "And place me among the inheritors of the Garden of Pleasure.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱجْعَلْنِى", "translit": "àِnْlَʿعْjgٱَw", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَرَثَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَhtَrَw", "root": "ورث"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "جَنَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلنَّعِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِʿعَّnlٱ", "root": "نعم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 86, "text": "وَٱغْفِرْ لِأَبِىٓ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلضَّآلِّينَ ", "translation": "And forgive my father. Indeed, he has been of those astray.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱغْفِرْ", "translit": "ْrِfْغٱَw", "root": "غفر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِأَبِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِbَaʾِl", "root": "ابو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلضَّآلِّينَ", "translit": "َnyِّlٓāَّḍlٱ", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 87, "text": "وَلَا تُخْزِنِى يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُونَ ", "translation": "And do not disgrace me on the Day they are [all] resurrected -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُخْزِنِى", "translit": "àِnِzْhkُt", "root": "خزي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُبْعَثُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhtَʿعْbُy", "root": "بعث"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 88, "text": "يَوْمَ لَا يَنفَعُ مَالٌ وَلَا بَنُونَ ", "translation": "The Day when there will not benefit [anyone] wealth or children", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَوْمَ", "translit": "َmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَنفَعُ", "translit": "ُʿعَfnَy", "root": "نفع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَالٌ", "translit": "ٌlāَm", "root": "مول"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnَb", "root": "بني"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 89, "text": "إِلَّا مَنْ أَتَى ٱللَّهَ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيمٍ ", "translation": "But only one who comes to Allāh with a sound heart.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَتَى", "translit": "àَtَaʾ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِقَلْبٍ", "translit": "ٍbْlَqِb", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "سَلِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِlَs", "root": "سلم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 90, "text": "وَأُزْلِفَتِ ٱلْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ ", "translation": "And Paradise will be brought near [that Day] to the righteous.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأُزْلِفَتِ", "translit": "ِtَfِlْzُaʾَw", "root": "زلف"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجَنَّةُ", "translit": "ُẗَّnَjgْlٱ", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِلْمُتَّقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqَّtُmْlِl", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 91, "text": "وَبُرِّزَتِ ٱلْجَحِيمُ لِلْغَاوِينَ ", "translation": "And Hellfire will be brought forth for the deviators,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَبُرِّزَتِ", "translit": "ِtَzِّrُbَw", "root": "برز"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْجَحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَjgْlٱ", "root": "جحم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِلْغَاوِينَ", "translit": "َnyِwāَغْlِl", "root": "غوي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 92, "text": "وَقِيلَ لَهُمْ أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُمْ تَعْبُدُونَ ", "translation": "And it will be said to them, \"Where are those you used to worship", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَقِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِqَw", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَيْنَ", "translit": "َnْyَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَعْبُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُbْʿعَt", "root": "عبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 93, "text": "مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ هَلْ يَنصُرُونَكُمْ أَوْ يَنتَصِرُونَ ", "translation": "Other than Allāh? Can they help you or help themselves?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُd", "root": "دون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَنصُرُونَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَnwُrُṣnَy", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَنتَصِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِṣَtnَy", "root": "نصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 94, "text": "فَكُبْكِبُوا۟ فِيهَا هُمْ وَٱلْغَاوُۥنَ ", "translation": "So they will be overturned into it [i.e., Hellfire], they and the deviators", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكُبْكِبُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُbِkْbُkَf", "root": "كبكب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلْغَاوُۥنَ", "translit": "َnۥُwāَغْlٱَw", "root": "غوي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 95, "text": "وَجُنُودُ إِبْلِيسَ أَجْمَعُونَ ", "translation": "And the soldiers of Iblees, all together.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجُنُودُ", "translit": "ُdwُnُjgَw", "root": "جند"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِبْلِيسَ", "translit": "َsyِlْbِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَجْمَعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 96, "text": "قَالُوا۟ وَهُمْ فِيهَا يَخْتَصِمُونَ ", "translation": "They will say while they dispute therein,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَخْتَصِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِṣَtْhkَy", "root": "خصم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 97, "text": "تَٱللَّهِ إِن كُنَّا لَفِى ضَلَٰلٍ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "\"By Allāh, we were indeed in manifest error", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱَt", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ضَلَٰلٍ", "translit": "ٍlَٰlَḍ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 98, "text": "إِذْ نُسَوِّيكُم بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "When we equated you with the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نُسَوِّيكُم", "translit": "mُkyِّwَsُn", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِرَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَrِb", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 99, "text": "وَمَآ أَضَلَّنَآ إِلَّا ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ ", "translation": "And no one misguided us except the criminals.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَضَلَّنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnَّlَḍَaʾ", "root": "ضلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُجْرِمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmِrْjgُmْlٱ", "root": "جرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 100, "text": "فَمَا لَنَا مِن شَٰفِعِينَ ", "translation": "So now we have no intercessors", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "شَٰفِعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعِfَٰhs", "root": "شفع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 101, "text": "وَلَا صَدِيقٍ حَمِيمٍ ", "translation": "And not a devoted friend.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "صَدِيقٍ", "translit": "ٍqyِdَṣ", "root": "صدق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَمِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِmَḥ", "root": "حمم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 102, "text": "فَلَوْ أَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةً فَنَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Then if we only had a return [to the world] and could be of the believers...\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَنَا", "translit": "āَnَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَرَّةً", "translit": "ًẗَّrَk", "root": "كرر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَنَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَnَf", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 103, "text": "إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 104, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 105, "text": "كَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ نُوحٍ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "The people of Noah denied the messengers[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَّبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نُوحٍ", "translit": "ٍḥwُn", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 106, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ أَخُوهُمْ نُوحٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "When their brother Noah said to them, \"Will you not fear Allāh?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَخُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "نُوحٌ", "translit": "ٌḥwُn", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 107, "text": "إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ", "translation": "Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَسُولٌ", "translit": "ٌlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 108, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 109, "text": "وَمَآ أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍۖ إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And I do not ask you for it any payment. My payment is only from the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٔـْsَaʾ", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرِىَ", "translit": "َàِrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 110, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 111, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ أَنُؤْمِنُ لَكَ وَٱتَّبَعَكَ ٱلْأَرْذَلُونَ ", "translation": "They said, \"Should we believe you while you are followed by the lowest [class of people]?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنُؤْمِنُ", "translit": "ُnِmْwʾُnَaʾ", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَكَ", "translit": "َkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱتَّبَعَكَ", "translit": "َkَʿعَbَّtٱَw", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْذَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَhdْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "رذل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 112, "text": "قَالَ وَمَا عِلْمِى بِمَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"And what is my knowledge of what they used to do?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عِلْمِى", "translit": "àِmْlِʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 113, "text": "إِنْ حِسَابُهُمْ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّىۖ لَوْ تَشْعُرُونَ ", "translation": "Their account is only upon my Lord, if you [could] perceive.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حِسَابُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُbāَsِḥ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبِّى", "translit": "àِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَوْ", "translit": "ْwَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَشْعُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُʿعْhsَt", "root": "شعر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 114, "text": "وَمَآ أَنَا۠ بِطَارِدِ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And I am not one to drive away the believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِطَارِدِ", "translit": "ِdِrāَṭِb", "root": "طرد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 115, "text": "إِنْ أَنَا۠ إِلَّا نَذِيرٌ مُّبِينٌ ", "translation": "I am only a clear warner.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنَا۠", "translit": "۠āَnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَذِيرٌ", "translit": "ٌryِhdَn", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مُّبِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 116, "text": "قَالُوا۟ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ يَٰنُوحُ لَتَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْمَرْجُومِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"If you do not desist, O Noah, you will surely be of those who are stoned.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَئِن", "translit": "nِyʾَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَنتَهِ", "translit": "ِhَtnَt", "root": "نهي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَٰنُوحُ", "translit": "ُḥwُnَٰy", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَتَكُونَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَnwُkَtَl", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْمَرْجُومِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmwُjgْrَmْlٱ", "root": "رجم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 117, "text": "قَالَ رَبِّ إِنَّ قَوْمِى كَذَّبُونِ ", "translation": "He said, \"My Lord, indeed my people have denied me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَوْمِى", "translit": "àِmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَذَّبُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 118, "text": "فَٱفْتَحْ بَيْنِى وَبَيْنَهُمْ فَتْحًا وَنَجِّنِى وَمَن مَّعِىَ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Then judge between me and them with decisive judgement and save me and those with me of the believers.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱفْتَحْ", "translit": "ْḥَtْfٱَf", "root": "فتح"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَيْنِى", "translit": "àِnْyَb", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَبَيْنَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَnْyَbَw", "root": "بين"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَتْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْtَf", "root": "فتح"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَنَجِّنِى", "translit": "àِnِّjgَnَw", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مَّعِىَ", "translit": "َàِʿعَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 119, "text": "فَأَنجَيْنَٰهُ وَمَن مَّعَهُۥ فِى ٱلْفُلْكِ ٱلْمَشْحُونِ ", "translation": "So We saved him and those with him in the laden ship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَنجَيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَjgnَaʾَf", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَن", "translit": "nَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّعَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَʿعَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْفُلْكِ", "translit": "ِkْlُfْlٱ", "root": "فلك"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمَشْحُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُḥْhsَmْlٱ", "root": "شحن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 120, "text": "ثُمَّ أَغْرَقْنَا بَعْدُ ٱلْبَاقِينَ ", "translation": "Then We drowned thereafter the remaining ones.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَغْرَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَrْغَaʾ", "root": "غرق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَعْدُ", "translit": "ُdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَاقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqāَbْlٱ", "root": "بقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 121, "text": "إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 122, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 123, "text": "كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "ʿAad denied the messengers", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَّبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَادٌ", "translit": "ٌdāَʿع", "root": "عود"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 124, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ أَخُوهُمْ هُودٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "When their brother Hūd said to them, \"Will you not fear Allāh?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَخُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "هُودٌ", "translit": "ٌdwُh", "root": "هود"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 125, "text": "إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ", "translation": "Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَسُولٌ", "translit": "ٌlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 126, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 127, "text": "وَمَآ أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍۖ إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And I do not ask you for it any payment. My payment is only from the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٔـْsَaʾ", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرِىَ", "translit": "َàِrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 128, "text": "أَتَبْنُونَ بِكُلِّ رِيعٍ ءَايَةً تَعْبَثُونَ ", "translation": "Do you construct on every elevation a sign,[1] amusing yourselves,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَتَبْنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnْbَtَaʾ", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِكُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُkِb", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رِيعٍ", "translit": "ٍʿعyِr", "root": "ريع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَعْبَثُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhtَbْʿعَt", "root": "عبث"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 129, "text": "وَتَتَّخِذُونَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُونَ ", "translation": "And take for yourselves constructions [i.e., palaces and fortresses] that you might abide eternally?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَتَّخِذُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhdِhkَّtَtَw", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَصَانِعَ", "translit": "َʿعِnāَṣَm", "root": "صنع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَعَلَّكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَّlَʿعَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَخْلُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُlْhkَt", "root": "خلد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 130, "text": "وَإِذَا بَطَشْتُم بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِينَ ", "translation": "And when you strike, you strike as tyrants.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَطَشْتُم", "translit": "mُtْhsَṭَb", "root": "بطش"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بَطَشْتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtْhsَṭَb", "root": "بطش"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "جَبَّارِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrāَّbَjg", "root": "جبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 131, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 132, "text": "وَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَمَدَّكُم بِمَا تَعْلَمُونَ ", "translation": "And fear He who provided you with that which you know,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَw", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَمَدَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّdَmَaʾ", "root": "مدد"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَعْلَمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmَlْʿعَt", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 133, "text": "أَمَدَّكُم بِأَنْعَٰمٍ وَبَنِينَ ", "translation": "Provided you with grazing livestock and children", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَمَدَّكُم", "translit": "mُkَّdَmَaʾ", "root": "مدد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِأَنْعَٰمٍ", "translit": "ٍmَٰʿعْnَaʾِb", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَبَنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnَbَw", "root": "بني"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 134, "text": "وَجَنَّٰتٍ وَعُيُونٍ ", "translation": "And gardens and springs.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَجَنَّٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَّٰnَjgَw", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَعُيُونٍ", "translit": "ٍnwُyُʿعَw", "root": "عين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 135, "text": "إِنِّىٓ أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ", "translation": "Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a terrible day.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَخَافُ", "translit": "ُfāَhkَaʾ", "root": "خوف"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "عَظِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 136, "text": "قَالُوا۟ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْنَآ أَوَعَظْتَ أَمْ لَمْ تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلْوَٰعِظِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"It is all the same to us whether you advise or are not of the advisors.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَوَآءٌ", "translit": "ٌءٓāَwَs", "root": "سوي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَوَعَظْتَ", "translit": "َtْẓَʿعَwَaʾ", "root": "وعظ"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَمْ", "translit": "ْmَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَمْ", "translit": "ْmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَكُن", "translit": "nُkَt", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْوَٰعِظِينَ", "translit": "َnyِẓِʿعَٰwْlٱ", "root": "وعظ"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 137, "text": "إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا خُلُقُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "This is not but the custom of the former peoples,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰذَآ", "translit": "ٓāَhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "خُلُقُ", "translit": "ُqُlُhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 138, "text": "وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِينَ ", "translation": "And we are not to be punished.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمُعَذَّبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَّhdَʿعُmِb", "root": "عذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 139, "text": "فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَهْلَكْنَٰهُمْۗ إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And they denied him, so We destroyed them. Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكَذَّبُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُbَّhdَkَf", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَأَهْلَكْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْkَlْhَaʾَf", "root": "هلك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 140, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 141, "text": "كَذَّبَتْ ثَمُودُ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "Thamūd denied the messengers", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَّبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ثَمُودُ", "translit": "ُdwُmَht", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 142, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ أَخُوهُمْ صَٰلِحٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "When their brother Ṣāliḥ said to them, \"Will you not fear Allāh?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَخُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "صَٰلِحٌ", "translit": "ٌḥِlَٰṣ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 143, "text": "إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ", "translation": "Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَسُولٌ", "translit": "ٌlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 144, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 145, "text": "وَمَآ أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍۖ إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And I do not ask you for it any payment. My payment is only from the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٔـْsَaʾ", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرِىَ", "translit": "َàِrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 146, "text": "أَتُتْرَكُونَ فِى مَا هَٰهُنَآ ءَامِنِينَ ", "translation": "Will you be left in what is here, secure [from death],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَتُتْرَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَrْtُtَaʾ", "root": "ترك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هَٰهُنَآ", "translit": "ٓāَnُhَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَامِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmāَء", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 147, "text": "فِى جَنَّٰتٍ وَعُيُونٍ ", "translation": "Within gardens and springs", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَنَّٰتٍ", "translit": "ٍtَّٰnَjg", "root": "جنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَعُيُونٍ", "translit": "ٍnwُyُʿعَw", "root": "عين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 148, "text": "وَزُرُوعٍ وَنَخْلٍ طَلْعُهَا هَضِيمٌ ", "translation": "And fields of crops and palm trees with softened fruit?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَزُرُوعٍ", "translit": "ٍʿعwُrُzَw", "root": "زرع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَنَخْلٍ", "translit": "ٍlْhkَnَw", "root": "نخل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "طَلْعُهَا", "translit": "āَhُʿعْlَṭ", "root": "طلع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هَضِيمٌ", "translit": "ٌmyِḍَh", "root": "هضم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 149, "text": "وَتَنْحِتُونَ مِنَ ٱلْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا فَٰرِهِينَ ", "translation": "And you carve out of the mountains, homes, with skill.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَنْحِتُونَ", "translit": "َnwُtِḥْnَtَw", "root": "نحت"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْجِبَالِ", "translit": "ِlāَbِjgْlٱ", "root": "جبل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بُيُوتًا", "translit": "āًtwُyُb", "root": "بيت"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "فَٰرِهِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhِrَٰf", "root": "فره"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 150, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 151, "text": "وَلَا تُطِيعُوٓا۟ أَمْرَ ٱلْمُسْرِفِينَ ", "translation": "And do not obey the order of the transgressors,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تُطِيعُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُʿعyِṭُt", "root": "طوع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَمْرَ", "translit": "َrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْرِفِينَ", "translit": "َnyِfِrْsُmْlٱ", "root": "سرف"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 152, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ يُفْسِدُونَ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَا يُصْلِحُونَ ", "translation": "Who cause corruption in the land and do not amend.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُفْسِدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdِsْfُy", "root": "فسد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُصْلِحُونَ", "translit": "َnwُḥِlْṣُy", "root": "صلح"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 153, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّمَآ أَنتَ مِنَ ٱلْمُسَحَّرِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"You are only of those affected by magic.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسَحَّرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَّḥَsُmْlٱ", "root": "سحر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 154, "text": "مَآ أَنتَ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا فَأْتِ بِـَٔايَةٍ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "You are but a man like ourselves, so bring a sign, if you should be of the truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَشَرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَhsَb", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّثْلُنَا", "translit": "āَnُlْhtِّm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "فَأْتِ", "translit": "ِtْaʾَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِـَٔايَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyāَٔـِb", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "كُنتَ", "translit": "َtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 155, "text": "قَالَ هَٰذِهِۦ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ ", "translation": "He said, \"This is a she-camel.[1] For her is a [time of] drink, and for you is a [time of] drink, [each] on a known day.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَٰذِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِhdَٰh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَاقَةٌ", "translit": "ٌẗَqāَn", "root": "نوق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَّهَا", "translit": "āَhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "شِرْبٌ", "translit": "ٌbْrِhs", "root": "شرب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَلَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "شِرْبُ", "translit": "ُbْrِhs", "root": "شرب"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَّعْلُومٍ", "translit": "ٍmwُlْʿعَّm", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 156, "text": "وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوٓءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ", "translation": "And do not touch her with harm, lest you be seized by the punishment of a terrible day.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَمَسُّوهَا", "translit": "āَhwُّsَmَt", "root": "مسس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِسُوٓءٍ", "translit": "ٍءٓwُsِb", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَhdُhkْaʾَyَf", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَذَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَظِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 157, "text": "فَعَقَرُوهَا فَأَصْبَحُوا۟ نَٰدِمِينَ ", "translation": "But they hamstrung her and so became regretful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَعَقَرُوهَا", "translit": "āَhwُrَqَʿعَf", "root": "عقر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَأَصْبَحُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُḥَbْṣَaʾَf", "root": "صبح"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَٰدِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِdَٰn", "root": "ندم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 158, "text": "فَأَخَذَهُمُ ٱلْعَذَابُۗ إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And the punishment seized them. Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَخَذَهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhَhdَhkَaʾَf", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 159, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 160, "text": "كَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوطٍ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "The people of Lot denied the messengers", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَّبَتْ", "translit": "ْtَbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَوْمُ", "translit": "ُmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لُوطٍ", "translit": "ٍṭwُl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 161, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ أَخُوهُمْ لُوطٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "When their brother Lot said to them, \"Will you not fear Allāh?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَخُوهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhwُhkَaʾ", "root": "اخو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لُوطٌ", "translit": "ٌṭwُl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 162, "text": "إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ", "translation": "Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَسُولٌ", "translit": "ٌlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 163, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 164, "text": "وَمَآ أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍۖ إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And I do not ask you for it any payment. My payment is only from the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٔـْsَaʾ", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرِىَ", "translit": "َàِrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 165, "text": "أَتَأْتُونَ ٱلذُّكْرَانَ مِنَ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "Do you approach males among the worlds[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَتَأْتُونَ", "translit": "َnwُtْaʾَtَaʾ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلذُّكْرَانَ", "translit": "َnāَrْkُّhdlٱ", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 166, "text": "وَتَذَرُونَ مَا خَلَقَ لَكُمْ رَبُّكُم مِّنْ أَزْوَٰجِكُمۚ بَلْ أَنتُمْ قَوْمٌ عَادُونَ ", "translation": "And leave what your Lord has created for you as mates? But you are a people transgressing.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَذَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَhdَtَw", "root": "وذر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَلَقَ", "translit": "َqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "رَبُّكُم", "translit": "mُkُّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَزْوَٰجِكُم", "translit": "mُkِjgَٰwْzَaʾ", "root": "زوج"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَلْ", "translit": "ْlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَنتُمْ", "translit": "ْmُtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "قَوْمٌ", "translit": "ٌmْwَq", "root": "قوم"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "عَادُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdāَʿع", "root": "عدو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 167, "text": "قَالُوا۟ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهِ يَٰلُوطُ لَتَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْمُخْرَجِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"If you do not desist, O Lot, you will surely be of those evicted.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَئِن", "translit": "nِyʾَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَنتَهِ", "translit": "ِhَtnَt", "root": "نهي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَٰلُوطُ", "translit": "ُṭwُlَٰy", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَتَكُونَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَnwُkَtَl", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْرَجِينَ", "translit": "َnyِjgَrْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خرج"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 168, "text": "قَالَ إِنِّى لِعَمَلِكُم مِّنَ ٱلْقَالِينَ ", "translation": "He said, \"Indeed, I am, toward your deed, of those who detest [it].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِعَمَلِكُم", "translit": "mُkِlَmَʿعِl", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَالِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlāَqْlٱ", "root": "قلي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 169, "text": "رَبِّ نَجِّنِى وَأَهْلِى مِمَّا يَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "My Lord, save me and my family from [the consequence of] what they do.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَجِّنِى", "translit": "àِnِّjgَn", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَهْلِى", "translit": "àِlْhَaʾَw", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَy", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 170, "text": "فَنَجَّيْنَٰهُ وَأَهْلَهُۥٓ أَجْمَعِينَ ", "translation": "So We saved him and his family, all,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَنَجَّيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَّjgَnَf", "root": "نجو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَأَهْلَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَlْhَaʾَw", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَجْمَعِينَ", "translit": "َnyِʿعَmْjgَaʾ", "root": "جمع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 171, "text": "إِلَّا عَجُوزًا فِى ٱلْغَٰبِرِينَ ", "translation": "Except an old woman[1] among those who remained behind.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَجُوزًا", "translit": "āًzwُjgَʿع", "root": "عجز"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْغَٰبِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِbَٰغْlٱ", "root": "غبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 172, "text": "ثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ ", "translation": "Then We destroyed the others.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "دَمَّرْنَا", "translit": "āَnْrَّmَd", "root": "دمر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْءَاخَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhkāَءْlٱ", "root": "اخر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 173, "text": "وَأَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِم مَّطَرًاۖ فَسَآءَ مَطَرُ ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ ", "translation": "And We rained upon them a rain [of stones], and evil was the rain of those who were warned.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَمْطَرْنَا", "translit": "āَnْrَṭْmَaʾَw", "root": "مطر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّطَرًا", "translit": "āًrَṭَّm", "root": "مطر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فَسَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَsَf", "root": "سوا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَطَرُ", "translit": "ُrَṭَm", "root": "مطر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنذَرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَhdnُmْlٱ", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 174, "text": "إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 175, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 176, "text": "كَذَّبَ أَصْحَٰبُ لْـَٔيْكَةِ ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ ", "translation": "The companions of the thicket [i.e., the people of Madyan] denied the messengers", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَّبَ", "translit": "َbَّhdَk", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لْـَٔيْكَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَkْyَٔـْl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَsْrُmْlٱ", "root": "رسل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 177, "text": "إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ شُعَيْبٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ", "translation": "When Shuʿayb said to them, \"Will you not fear Allāh?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذْ", "translit": "ْhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "شُعَيْبٌ", "translit": "ٌbْyَʿعُhs", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَلَا", "translit": "āَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَتَّقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqَّtَt", "root": "وقي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 178, "text": "إِنِّى لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ", "translation": "Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَسُولٌ", "translit": "ٌlwُsَr", "root": "رسل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَمِينٌ", "translit": "ٌnyِmَaʾ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 179, "text": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ", "translation": "So fear Allāh and obey me.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَf", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَطِيعُونِ", "translit": "ِnwُʿعyِṭَaʾَw", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 180, "text": "وَمَآ أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍۖ إِنْ أَجْرِىَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And I do not ask you for it any payment. My payment is only from the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَسْـَٔلُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُlَٔـْsَaʾ", "root": "سال"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنْ", "translit": "ْnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَجْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرِىَ", "translit": "َàِrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 181, "text": "أَوْفُوا۟ ٱلْكَيْلَ وَلَا تَكُونُوا۟ مِنَ ٱلْمُخْسِرِينَ ", "translation": "Give full measure and do not be of those who cause loss.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوْفُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُfْwَaʾ", "root": "وفي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْكَيْلَ", "translit": "َlْyَkْlٱ", "root": "كيل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَكُونُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnwُkَt", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُخْسِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِsْhkُmْlٱ", "root": "خسر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 182, "text": "وَزِنُوا۟ بِٱلْقِسْطَاسِ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمِ ", "translation": "And weigh with an even [i.e., honest] balance.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَزِنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnِzَw", "root": "وزن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِٱلْقِسْطَاسِ", "translit": "ِsāَṭْsِqْlٱِb", "root": "قسطس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِqَtْsُmْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 183, "text": "وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا۟ ٱلنَّاسَ أَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا۟ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ ", "translation": "And do not deprive people of their due and do not commit abuse on earth, spreading corruption.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَبْخَسُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُsَhkْbَt", "root": "بخس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلنَّاسَ", "translit": "َsāَّnlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَشْيَآءَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَءٓāَyْhsَaʾ", "root": "شيا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "تَعْثَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَhtْʿعَt", "root": "عثو"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مُفْسِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِsْfُm", "root": "فسد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 184, "text": "وَٱتَّقُوا۟ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَكُمْ وَٱلْجِبِلَّةَ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "And fear He who created you and the former creation.\"[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱتَّقُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُqَّtٱَw", "root": "وقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَلَقَكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkَqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَٱلْجِبِلَّةَ", "translit": "َẗَّlِbِjgْlٱَw", "root": "جبل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 185, "text": "قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّمَآ أَنتَ مِنَ ٱلْمُسَحَّرِينَ ", "translation": "They said, \"You are only of those affected by magic.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسَحَّرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrَّḥَsُmْlٱ", "root": "سحر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 186, "text": "وَمَآ أَنتَ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا وَإِن نَّظُنُّكَ لَمِنَ ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ ", "translation": "You are but a man like ourselves, and indeed, we think you are among the liars.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَشَرٌ", "translit": "ٌrَhsَb", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِّثْلُنَا", "translit": "āَnُlْhtِّm", "root": "مثل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَإِن", "translit": "nِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "نَّظُنُّكَ", "translit": "َkُّnُẓَّn", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "لَمِنَ", "translit": "َnِmَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْكَٰذِبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbِhdَٰkْlٱ", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 187, "text": "فَأَسْقِطْ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ", "translation": "So cause to fall upon us fragments of the sky, if you should be of the truthful.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَسْقِطْ", "translit": "ْṭِqْsَaʾَf", "root": "سقط"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْنَا", "translit": "āَnْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كِسَفًا", "translit": "āًfَsِk", "root": "كسف"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنَ", "translit": "َnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءِ", "translit": "ِءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كُنتَ", "translit": "َtnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ", "translit": "َnyِqِdَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صدق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 188, "text": "قَالَ رَبِّىٓ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "He said, \"My Lord is most knowing of what you do.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "قَالَ", "translit": "َlāَq", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبِّىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَt", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 189, "text": "فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَخَذَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمِ ٱلظُّلَّةِۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ", "translation": "And they denied him, so the punishment of the day of the black cloud seized them. Indeed, it was the punishment of a terrible day.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكَذَّبُوهُ", "translit": "ُhwُbَّhdَkَf", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فَأَخَذَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَhdَhkَaʾَf", "root": "اخذ"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَذَابُ", "translit": "ُbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلظُّلَّةِ", "translit": "ِẗَّlُّẓlٱ", "root": "ظلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "عَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿع", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "عَظِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِẓَʿع", "root": "عظم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 190, "text": "إِنَّ فِى ذَٰلِكَ لَءَايَةًۖ وَمَا كَانَ أَكْثَرُهُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "Indeed in that is a sign, but most of them were not to be believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَءَl", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَكْثَرُهُم", "translit": "mُhُrَhtْkَaʾ", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مُّؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُّm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 191, "text": "وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ", "translation": "And indeed, your Lord - He is the Exalted in Might, the Merciful.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَبَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُوَ", "translit": "َwُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزُ", "translit": "ُzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 192, "text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ لَتَنزِيلُ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, it [i.e., the Qur’ān] is the revelation of the Lord of the worlds.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَتَنزِيلُ", "translit": "ُlyِznَtَl", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 193, "text": "نَزَلَ بِهِ ٱلرُّوحُ ٱلْأَمِينُ ", "translation": "The Trustworthy Spirit [i.e., Gabriel] has brought it down", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "نَزَلَ", "translit": "َlَzَn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِهِ", "translit": "ِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلرُّوحُ", "translit": "ُḥwُّrlٱ", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَمِينُ", "translit": "ُnyِmَaʾْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 194, "text": "عَلَىٰ قَلْبِكَ لِتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلْمُنذِرِينَ ", "translation": "Upon your heart, [O Muḥammad] - that you may be of the warners", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قَلْبِكَ", "translit": "َkِbْlَq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِتَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَtِl", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُنذِرِينَ", "translit": "َnyِrِhdnُmْlٱ", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 195, "text": "بِلِسَانٍ عَرَبِىٍّ مُّبِينٍ ", "translation": "In a clear Arabic language.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بِلِسَانٍ", "translit": "ٍnāَsِlِb", "root": "لسن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَرَبِىٍّ", "translit": "ٍّàِbَrَʿع", "root": "عرب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُّبِينٍ", "translit": "ٍnyِbُّm", "root": "بين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 196, "text": "وَإِنَّهُۥ لَفِى زُبُرِ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ ", "translation": "And indeed, it is [mentioned] in the scriptures of former peoples.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَفِى", "translit": "àِfَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "زُبُرِ", "translit": "ِrُbُz", "root": "زبر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ", "translit": "َnyِlَّwَaʾْlٱ", "root": "اول"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 197, "text": "أَوَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُمْ ءَايَةً أَن يَعْلَمَهُۥ عُلَمَٰٓؤُا۟ بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ ", "translation": "And has it not been a sign to them that it is recognized by the scholars of the Children of Israel?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَكُن", "translit": "nُkَy", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ءَايَةً", "translit": "ًẗَyāَء", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَعْلَمَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَmَlْʿعَy", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عُلَمَٰٓؤُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwʾَٰٓmَlُʿع", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "بَنِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِnَb", "root": "بني"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ", "translit": "َlyِءَٰٓrْsِiʾ", "root": ""}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 198, "text": "وَلَوْ نَزَّلْنَٰهُ عَلَىٰ بَعْضِ ٱلْأَعْجَمِينَ ", "translation": "And even if We had revealed it to one among the foreigners[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَوْ", "translit": "ْwَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَزَّلْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْlَّzَn", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بَعْضِ", "translit": "ِḍْʿعَb", "root": "بعض"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْأَعْجَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَjgْʿعَaʾْlٱ", "root": "عجم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 199, "text": "فَقَرَأَهُۥ عَلَيْهِم مَّا كَانُوا۟ بِهِۦ مُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And he had recited it to them [perfectly],[1] they would [still] not have been believers in it.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَقَرَأَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَaʾَrَqَf", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِم", "translit": "mِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُm", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 200, "text": "كَذَٰلِكَ سَلَكْنَٰهُ فِى قُلُوبِ ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ ", "translation": "Thus have We inserted it [i.e., disbelief] into the hearts of the criminals.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "كَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَk", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَلَكْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْkَlَs", "root": "سلك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قُلُوبِ", "translit": "ِbwُlُq", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِrْjgُmْlٱ", "root": "جرم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 201, "text": "لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِهِۦ حَتَّىٰ يَرَوُا۟ ٱلْعَذَابَ ٱلْأَلِيمَ ", "translation": "They will not believe in it until they see the painful punishment.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَرَوُا۟", "translit": "۟āُwَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْعَذَابَ", "translit": "َbāَhdَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱلْأَلِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِlَaʾْlٱ", "root": "الم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 202, "text": "فَيَأْتِيَهُم بَغْتَةً وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ", "translation": "And it will come to them suddenly while they perceive [it] not.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَيَأْتِيَهُم", "translit": "mُhَyِtْaʾَyَf", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بَغْتَةً", "translit": "ًẗَtْغَb", "root": "بغت"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَشْعُرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrُʿعْhsَy", "root": "شعر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 203, "text": "فَيَقُولُوا۟ هَلْ نَحْنُ مُنظَرُونَ ", "translation": "And they will say, \"May we be reprieved?\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَيَقُولُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlwُqَyَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "نَحْنُ", "translit": "ُnْḥَn", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مُنظَرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrَẓnُm", "root": "نظر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 204, "text": "أَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ ", "translation": "So for Our punishment are they impatient?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَبِعَذَابِنَا", "translit": "āَnِbāَhdَʿعِbَfَaʾ", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَسْتَعْجِلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlِjgْʿعَtْsَy", "root": "عجل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 205, "text": "أَفَرَءَيْتَ إِن مَّتَّعْنَٰهُمْ سِنِينَ ", "translation": "Then have you considered if We gave them enjoyment for years", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَفَرَءَيْتَ", "translit": "َtْyَءَrَfَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِن", "translit": "nِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّتَّعْنَٰهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَٰnْʿعَّtَّm", "root": "متع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "سِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِs", "root": "سنو"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 206, "text": "ثُمَّ جَآءَهُم مَّا كَانُوا۟ يُوعَدُونَ ", "translation": "And then there came to them that which they were promised?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَآءَهُم", "translit": "mُhَءٓāَjg", "root": "جيا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يُوعَدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdَʿعwُy", "root": "وعد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 207, "text": "مَآ أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُم مَّا كَانُوا۟ يُمَتَّعُونَ ", "translation": "They would not be availed by the enjoyment with which they were provided.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَآ", "translit": "ٓāَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَغْنَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَnْغَaʾ", "root": "غني"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَنْهُم", "translit": "mُhْnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَّا", "translit": "āَّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَانُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يُمَتَّعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَّtَmُy", "root": "متع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 208, "text": "وَمَآ أَهْلَكْنَا مِن قَرْيَةٍ إِلَّا لَهَا مُنذِرُونَ ", "translation": "And We did not destroy any city except that it had warners", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَهْلَكْنَا", "translit": "āَnْkَlْhَaʾ", "root": "هلك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِن", "translit": "nِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "قَرْيَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَyْrَq", "root": "قري"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَهَا", "translit": "āَhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مُنذِرُونَ", "translit": "َnwُrِhdnُm", "root": "نذر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 209, "text": "ذِكْرَىٰ وَمَا كُنَّا ظَٰلِمِينَ ", "translation": "As a reminder; and never have We been unjust.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ذِكْرَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَrْkِhd", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُنَّا", "translit": "āَّnُk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ظَٰلِمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmِlَٰẓ", "root": "ظلم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 210, "text": "وَمَا تَنَزَّلَتْ بِهِ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينُ ", "translation": "And the devils have not brought it [i.e., the revelation] down.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَنَزَّلَتْ", "translit": "ْtَlَّzَnَt", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهِ", "translit": "ِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيَٰطِينُ", "translit": "ُnyِṭَٰyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 211, "text": "وَمَا يَنۢبَغِى لَهُمْ وَمَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ ", "translation": "It is not allowable for them, nor would they be able.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَنۢبَغِى", "translit": "àِغَbۢnَy", "root": "بغي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَسْتَطِيعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعyِṭَtْsَy", "root": "طوع"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 212, "text": "إِنَّهُمْ عَنِ ٱلسَّمْعِ لَمَعْزُولُونَ ", "translation": "Indeed they, from [its] hearing, are removed.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَنِ", "translit": "ِnَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمْعِ", "translit": "ِʿعْmَّslٱ", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَمَعْزُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُzْʿعَmَl", "root": "عزل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 213, "text": "فَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَٰهًا ءَاخَرَ فَتَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلْمُعَذَّبِينَ ", "translation": "So do not invoke[1] with Allāh another deity and [thus] be among the punished.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَدْعُ", "translit": "ُʿعْdَt", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَعَ", "translit": "َʿعَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَٰهًا", "translit": "āًhَٰlِiʾ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ءَاخَرَ", "translit": "َrَhkāَء", "root": "اخر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "فَتَكُونَ", "translit": "َnwُkَtَf", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلْمُعَذَّبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَّhdَʿعُmْlٱ", "root": "عذب"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 214, "text": "وَأَنذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ ٱلْأَقْرَبِينَ ", "translation": "And warn, [O Muḥammad], your closest kindred.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنذِرْ", "translit": "ْrِhdnَaʾَw", "root": "نذر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَشِيرَتَكَ", "translit": "َkَtَryِhsَʿع", "root": "عشر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْأَقْرَبِينَ", "translit": "َnyِbَrْqَaʾْlٱ", "root": "قرب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 215, "text": "وَٱخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ ", "translation": "And lower your wing [i.e., show kindness] to those who follow you of the believers.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱخْفِضْ", "translit": "ْḍِfْhkٱَw", "root": "خفض"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "جَنَاحَكَ", "translit": "َkَḥāَnَjg", "root": "جنح"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لِمَنِ", "translit": "ِnَmِl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱتَّبَعَكَ", "translit": "َkَʿعَbَّtٱ", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ", "translit": "َnyِnِmْwʾُmْlٱ", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 216, "text": "فَإِنْ عَصَوْكَ فَقُلْ إِنِّى بَرِىٓءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ ", "translation": "And if they disobey you, then say, \"Indeed, I am disassociated from what you are doing.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَإِنْ", "translit": "ْnِiʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَصَوْكَ", "translit": "َkْwَṣَʿع", "root": "عصي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فَقُلْ", "translit": "ْlُqَf", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "إِنِّى", "translit": "àِّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بَرِىٓءٌ", "translit": "ٌءٓàِrَb", "root": "برا"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مِّمَّا", "translit": "āَّmِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "تَعْمَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَmْʿعَt", "root": "عمل"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 217, "text": "وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ", "translation": "And rely upon the Exalted in Might, the Merciful,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَوَكَّلْ", "translit": "ْlَّkَwَtَw", "root": "وكل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَى", "translit": "àَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعَزِيزِ", "translit": "ِzyِzَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عزز"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 218, "text": "ٱلَّذِى يَرَىٰكَ حِينَ تَقُومُ ", "translation": "Who sees you when you arise[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حِينَ", "translit": "َnyِḥ", "root": "حين"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "تَقُومُ", "translit": "ُmwُqَt", "root": "قوم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 219, "text": "وَتَقَلُّبَكَ فِى ٱلسَّٰجِدِينَ ", "translation": "And your movement among those who prostrate.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَتَقَلُّبَكَ", "translit": "َkَbُّlَqَtَw", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّٰجِدِينَ", "translit": "َnyِdِjgَّٰslٱ", "root": "سجد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 220, "text": "إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ ", "translation": "Indeed, He is the Hearing, the Knowing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُوَ", "translit": "َwُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمِيعُ", "translit": "ُʿعyِmَّslٱ", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَلِيمُ", "translit": "ُmyِlَʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 221, "text": "هَلْ أُنَبِّئُكُمْ عَلَىٰ مَن تَنَزَّلُ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينُ ", "translation": "Shall I inform you upon whom the devils descend?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "هَلْ", "translit": "ْlَh", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أُنَبِّئُكُمْ", "translit": "ْmُkُyʾِّbَnُaʾ", "root": "نبا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَن", "translit": "nَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "تَنَزَّلُ", "translit": "ُlَّzَnَt", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلشَّيَٰطِينُ", "translit": "ُnyِṭَٰyَّhslٱ", "root": "شطن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 222, "text": "تَنَزَّلُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ أَفَّاكٍ أَثِيمٍ ", "translation": "They descend upon every sinful liar.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَنَزَّلُ", "translit": "ُlَّzَnَt", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَفَّاكٍ", "translit": "ٍkāَّfَaʾ", "root": "افك"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَثِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِhtَaʾ", "root": "اثم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 223, "text": "يُلْقُونَ ٱلسَّمْعَ وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ كَٰذِبُونَ ", "translation": "They pass on what is heard,[1] and most of them are liars.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يُلْقُونَ", "translit": "َnwُqْlُy", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمْعَ", "translit": "َʿعْmَّslٱ", "root": "سمع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَأَكْثَرُهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhُrَhtْkَaʾَw", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَٰذِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِhdَٰk", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 224, "text": "وَٱلشُّعَرَآءُ يَتَّبِعُهُمُ ٱلْغَاوُۥنَ ", "translation": "And the poets - [only] the deviators follow them.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلشُّعَرَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَrَʿعُّhslٱَw", "root": "شعر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَتَّبِعُهُمُ", "translit": "ُmُhُʿعِbَّtَy", "root": "تبع"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْغَاوُۥنَ", "translit": "َnۥُwāَغْlٱ", "root": "غوي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 225, "text": "أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّهُمْ فِى كُلِّ وَادٍ يَهِيمُونَ ", "translation": "Do you not see that in every valley they roam[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "تَرَ", "translit": "َrَt", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَادٍ", "translit": "ٍdāَw", "root": "ودي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "يَهِيمُونَ", "translit": "َnwُmyِhَy", "root": "هيم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 226, "text": "وَأَنَّهُمْ يَقُولُونَ مَا لَا يَفْعَلُونَ ", "translation": "And that they say what they do not do? -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنَّهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَّnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَقُولُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlwُqَy", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَفْعَلُونَ", "translit": "َnwُlَʿعْfَy", "root": "فعل"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 227, "text": "إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَذَكَرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ كَثِيرًا وَٱنتَصَرُوا۟ مِنۢ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوا۟ۗ وَسَيَعْلَمُ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُوٓا۟ أَىَّ مُنقَلَبٍ يَنقَلِبُونَ ", "translation": "Except those [poets] who believe and do righteous deeds and remember Allāh often and defend [the Muslims][1] after they were wronged. And those who have wronged are going to know to what [kind of] return they will be returned.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَذَكَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَkَhdَw", "root": "ذكر"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "ٱللَّهَ", "translit": "َhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كَثِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِhtَk", "root": "كثر"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "وَٱنتَصَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَṣَtnٱَw", "root": "نصر"}, {"id": 10, "arabic": "مِنۢ", "translit": "ۢnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 11, "arabic": "بَعْدِ", "translit": "ِdْʿعَb", "root": "بعد"}, {"id": 12, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 13, "arabic": "ظُلِمُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُmِlُẓ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 14, "arabic": "وَسَيَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَyَsَw", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 15, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 16, "arabic": "ظَلَمُوٓا۟", "translit": "۟āٓwُmَlَẓ", "root": "ظلم"}, {"id": 17, "arabic": "أَىَّ", "translit": "َّàَaʾ", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 18, "arabic": "مُنقَلَبٍ", "translit": "ٍbَlَqnُm", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 19, "arabic": "يَنقَلِبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِlَqnَy", "root": "قلب"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"12": [{"arabic": "في التعليل والاعتذار لما قيل له اذهب إلى فرعون {فقال} ولهم على ذنب وقوله إني أخاف أن يكذبون ويضيق صدري ولا ينطلق لساني وقوله إننا نخاف أن يفرط علينا أو أن يطغى وهذا من غير موسى عليه السلام من سوء الأدب لأن الذي أقيم مقام الأنس يلاطف ويحتمل ولم يحتمل ليونس عليه السلام ما دون هذا لما أقيم مقام القبض والهيبة فعوقب بالسجن في بطن الحوت في ظلمات ثلاث ونودي عليه إلى يوم القيامة لولا أن تداركه نعمة من ربه لنبذ بالعراء وهو مذموم قال الحسن العراء هو القيامة ونهى نبينا صلى الله عليه وسلم أن يقتدى به وقيل له فاصبر لحكم ربك ولا تكن كصاحب الحوت إذ نادى وهو مكظوم وهذه الاختلا", "english": "As for Adam (peace be upon him), it was said concerning him: {«وعصى آدم ربه فغوى»} \"And Adam disobeyed his Lord, so he went astray\" (Q. 20:121), then {«اجتباه ربه فتاب عليه وهدى»} \"his Lord chose him, and turned to him in forgiveness, and guided him\" (Q. 20:122).", "book_title": "Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment", "section_title_ar": "Section 1187", "section_title_en": "On the Varieties of Divine Proximity (Al-Inbisāṭ) and Awe (Al-Haybah) in the States of the Prophets and Saints", "section_index": 1187, "anchors": "- Root: بسط (B-S-T)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is \"to spread out, extend, expand\" — both physically (basting a garment) and metaphorically.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance: \"بسط الشيء: نشره وتوسيعه\" — used for expansion of mercy, favor, and the soul's comfort. In Kalam, it contrasts with *qabḍ* (contraction/withholding).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"بسط الثوب والفراش إذا نشره.\" Metaphorical (Majaz): \"بسطني ما بسطك\" (what pleases you pleases me) — hence *inbisāṭ* here denotes the soul's expansive intimacy with God, a spiritual state, not a physical act.\n- Root: أبلس (B-L-S)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"أبلس: انقطعت حجته ويئس\" — to be reduced to silence, to despair.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الإبلاس: الحزن المعترض من شدة اليأس\" — the despair of Iblis is a theological state of being cut off from mercy.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: despair/silence. Metaphorical: Iblis (the proper name) is derived from this root — he is the one \"despairing\" of divine mercy.\n- Root: عله (not used; avoided per instruction) — *Note: The text's key term \"الإدلال\" (al-idlāl) is from root دلو (D-L-W).*\n- Root: دلو (D-L-W)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"دلا الدلو: أخرجها من البئر\" — to draw water from a well; hence *iddalā'a* (إدلال) means to advance boldly, relying on a familiar bond.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Not a primary Quranic term, but lexically implies confident approach based on prior intimacy.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: lowering the bucket. Metaphorical: \"أدلّ عليه\" — to act with bold familiarity toward someone who loves you, trusting in their affection.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Applied in the phrase \"فإنما هي عند ذوي الاعتبار من الأسماء\" (they are but names to those who reflect), restricting the ontological status of stories to mere signifiers for the discerning.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Love, Longing, Intimacy and Contentment'", "badge": "Insight"}], "23": [{"arabic": "جادلتنا فأكثرت جدالنا وقال تعالى في قصة فرعون وما رب العالمين إلى قوله أولوا جئتك بشيء مبين وعلى الجملة فالقرآن من أوله إلى آخره محاجة مع الكفار فعمدة أدلة المتكلمين في التوحيد قوله تعالى {لو كان فيهما آلهة إلا الله لفسدتا} وفي النبوة {وإن كنتم في ريب مما نزلنا على عبدنا فأتوا بسورة من مثله} وفي البعث {قل يحييها الذي أنشأها أول مرة} إلى غير ذلك من الآيات والأدلة ولم تزل الرسل صلوات الله عليهم يحاجون المنكرين ويجادلونهم قال تعالى {وجادلهم بالتي هي أحسن} فالصحابة رضي الله عنهم أيضا كانوا يحاجون المنكرين ويجاد", "english": "The mention of the proof (ḥujjah), the demand for it, and the search after it — how could these be prohibited, when God — may He be exalted — has said: {«قُلْ هَاتُوا بُرْهَانَكُمْ»} (Say: Bring forth your proof — Qur'an 2:111), and He — mighty and majestic — has said: {«لِيَهْلِكَ مَنْ هَلَكَ عَنْ بَيِّنَةٍ وَيَحْيَا مَنْ حَيَّ عَنْ بَيِّنَةٍ»} (So that he who perishes may perish upon clear evidence, and he who lives may live upon clear evidence — Qur'an 8:42), and He — may He be exalted — has said: {«هَلْ عِنْدَكُمْ مِنْ سُلْطَانٍ بِهَذَا»} (Have you any authority for this? — Qur'an 10:68), meaning a proof and demonstration, and He — may He be exalted — has said: {«قُلْ فَلِلَّهِ الْحُجَّةُ الْبَالِغَةُ»} (Say: To God belongs the conclusive proof — Qur'an 6:149), and He — may He be exalted — has said: {«أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِي حَاجَّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ فِي رَبِّهِ»} (Have you not considered him who disputed with Abraham concerning his Lord? — Qur'an 2:258) up to His words: {«فَبُهِتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ»} (So the one who disbelieved was confounded — Qur'an 2:258).", "book_title": "Foundations of Belief", "section_title_ar": "Section 77", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 77: On the Permissibility of Theological Discourse (Kalām) and Its Early Practice", "section_index": 77, "anchors": "- Root: ح-د-ث (ḥ-d-th)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Al-ḥudūth: the coming-to-be of a thing after it was not; al-ḥadath: the novel event; al-ḥīdāth: origination.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-ḥudūth: a thing's becoming after it was not, whether accident or substance; iḥdāth: bringing it into existence. The origination of substances belongs to God alone.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: 'He is a recent event among events.' Metaphorical: 'They became topics of conversation (aḥādīth).'\"\n- Root: ح-ا-ج (ḥ-ā-j)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Al-ḥājah: need of a thing, with desire for it; its plural: ḥājāt and ḥawā'ij.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-ḥājah ilā al-shay': poverty toward it with love of it. God said: {«إِلَّا حَاجَةً فِي نَفْسِ يَعْقُوبَ»} (except a need in Jacob's soul — Qur'an 12:68).\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: need and want. The 'ḥājah' is that which one seeks to obtain.\"\n- Root: ك-و-ن (k-w-n)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"Kāna: to be, to exist; takwīn: bringing into being from non-existence.\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-kawn: existence after non-existence; the muḥdath (originated thing) is that brought forth after it was not.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: being and becoming. Metaphorical: the continuous states of affairs.\"\n- Sibawayh Rule: Al-Faṣl bayna al-Jār wa-al-Majrūr (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of separating a preposition from its object when the intervening clause is complete in meaning, as in the verse's structure of argumentation where the proof (ḥujjah) stands independently before its conclusion.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Foundations of Belief'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "42": [{"arabic": "وسلم وإنكم إذا لمن المقربين والثاني يضاهي تعويد الصبي الذي يراد منه المصارعة والمقاتلة بمباشرة أسباب ذلك منذ الصبا حتى يأنس به ويستجرىء عليه وتقوى فيه منته فمن ترك بالكلية المجاهدة بالصبر ضعف فيه باعث الدين ولا يقوى على الشهوة وإن ضعفت ومن عود نفسه مخالفة الهوى غلبها مهما أراد فهذا منهاج العلاج في جميع أنواع الصبر ولا يمكن استيفاؤه وإنما أشدها كف الباطن عن حديث النفس وإنما يشتد ذلك على من تفرغ له بأن قمع الشهوات الظاهرة وآثر العزلة وجلس للمراقبة والذكر والفكر فإن الوسواس", "english": "Of its own kind [i.e., lawful food] that suffices in place of the forbidden things — and this is the most beneficial remedy for the majority of people. For cutting off food entirely weakens one for all other works, and moreover it may not quell the lust in the case of most men. That is why the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: «عليكم بالباءة فمن لم يستطع فعليه بالصوم فإن الصوم له وجاء» — \"Upon you is marriage; and whoever cannot [bear it], then upon him is fasting, for fasting is for him a castration [of lust].\"", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "section_title_ar": "Section 968", "section_title_en": "The Threefold Remedy for Lust and the Strengthening of the Religious Motive", "section_index": 968, "anchors": "- Root: صبر (ṣ-b-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Restraint and holding back in constriction; al-Raghib: \"حبس النفس على ما يقتضيه العقل والشرع\" — the soul's confinement to what reason and Law require.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Patience is a generic term (لفظ عام) whose names vary by context — in calamity it is ṣabr, in battle it is courage (shajāʿah), its opposite being impatience (jazaʿ).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"صبرت على ما أكره. وصبرت عما أحب\" — patience over the disliked and patience away from the beloved; metaphorical (majāz): \"هو أصبر على الضرب من الأرض\" — endurance likened to the earth's bearing of blows.\n- Root: قطع (q-ṭ-ʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Severing and separation of what is perceptible.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"القطع: فصل الشيء مدركا بالبصر أو بالبصيرة\" — severance of what is perceived by sight or by inner insight; includes cutting off food (قطع الغذاء) as physical severance of appetite's fuel.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: cutting limbs or cloth; metaphorical (majāz): \"قطع المفازة\" — crossing the desert, i.e., severing the journey's expanse; here, severing the animal appetite's supply.\n- Root: ثني (th-n-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Folding and doubling back.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الثني: ما يعاد مرتين\" — that which is repeated twice; the second cause \"يضاهي تغييب اللحم عن الكلب\" — concealing the stimulus so the appetite is not re-folded into arousal.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Metaphorical: \"ثنيت فلانا على وجهه إذا رجعته إلى حيث جاء\" — turning someone back; here, turning the soul away from the object of lust by removal from sight.\n- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, spirit, or breath; that which is precious (نفيس).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النفس: الروح\" and \"نفسه: ذاته\" — the self as the divine referent in God's case; for man, the soul as the seat of both appetites and the religious motive.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شيء نفيس ومنفس\" — a precious thing; metaphorical (majāz): \"دفق نفسه أي دمه\" — the self as the blood of life; here, \"أسلم خسيسا في نفيس\" — trading the base for the precious, the soul's true worth.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — \"إنما يكون بطريقين\" restricts the means of strengthening the religious motive to exactly two paths, excluding all others; \"لا علاج له البتة إلا قطع العلائق\" employs absolute restriction (البتة) with exception (إلا) to delimit the sole remedy.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Insight"}], "49": [{"arabic": "حقيقة الأمر فلم يكترثوا بقول فرعون لأقطعن أيديكم وأرجلكم من خلاف {بل} قالوا لن نؤثرك على ما جاءنا من البينات والذي فطرنا قاقض ما أنت قاض إنما تقضي هذه الحياة الدنيا فإن البيان والكشف يمنع التغيير وأما أصحاب السامري لما كان إيمانهم عن النظر إلى ظاهر الثعبان فلما نظروا إلى عجل السامري وسمعوا خواره تغيروا وسمعوا قوله هذا إلهكم وإله موسى ونسوا أنه لا يرجع إليهم قولا ولا يملك لهم ضرا ولا نفعا فكل من آمن بالنظر إلى ثعبان يكفر لا محالة إذا نظر إلى عجل لأن كليهما من عالم الشهادة والاختلاف والتضاد في عالم الشهادة كثير", "english": "...its mover is Power (al-qudrah) without any doubt. So the seeker (al-sālik) journeyed on to the world of Power, and there he beheld wonders before which all that had preceded seemed contemptible. He asked Power concerning the movement of the right hand, and it said: \"I am but an attribute (innamā anā ṣifah) — ask the Powerful One (al-Qādir), for the reliance is upon the described substances (al-mawṣūfāt), not upon the attributes.\" At that point he almost deviated and unleashed the tongue of questioning with audacity, but he was steadied by the firm word (al-qawl al-thābit), and a caller cried out from behind the veils of the pavilions of the Divine Presence: \"He is not asked about what He does, but they shall be asked\" {«لَا يُسْأَلُ عَمَّا يَفْعَلُ وَهُمْ يُسْأَلُونَ»}. Then the awe of the Presence overwhelmed him, and he fell down stricken, convulsing in his swoon. When he regained consciousness, he said: \"Glory be to You — how magnificent is Your majesty! I repent unto You, and I place my trust in You, and I believe that You are the Sovereign, the Compeller, the One, the Subduer. I fear none but You, I hope for none other than You, and I seek refuge only in Your pardon from Your punishment, and in Your good pleasure from Your wrath. I have nothing but to ask of You and to supplicate before You, and to plead humbly in Your presence, saying: 'Expand my breast that I may know You, and loosen the knot from my tongue that I may praise You.'\"", "book_title": "Monotheism and Reliance", "section_title_ar": "Section 1111", "section_title_en": "The Unification of the Acts — The Journey of the Seekers to the Oneness of the Agent", "section_index": 1111, "anchors": "- Root: قدر (q-d-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of measuring, determining, and empowering; al-Qadir as the One whose power is absolute and unbounded.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Power (qudrah) when ascribed to God is the negation of incapacity ('ajz); when ascribed to man it is a contingent capacity limited by divine ordainment.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqiqah) — \"He is Qadir, Muqtadir, possessor of power\"; metaphorical (majaz) — \"a far-reaching steed\" (ba'id al-qadr), indicating extension of effect.\n- Root: وحد (w-ḥ-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Oneness and singularity; al-Wahid as that which has no part whatsoever.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): True unity (wahdah) is absolute indivisibility; applied to God exclusively in the sense of unique sovereignty.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"He is one (wahid), and they are singular (wuhdan)\"; literal unity versus numerical oneness.\n- Root: علم (ʿ-l-m)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowledge as perception of a thing's reality; the mark or sign by which something is known.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Knowledge ('ilm) is the apprehension of a thing in its true reality — either grasping the essence or judging its attributes.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — \"I knew not of your news\" (ma 'alimtu bi-khabarika); the knower as one marked by discernment.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Restriction and Focused Predication (al-ḥaṣr wa al-taqyīd bi-innamā) — \"Innamā anā ṣifah\" (I am but an attribute) restricts the speaker's essence to being a mere accident, redirecting inquiry to the substantive subject (al-mawṣūf).", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Monotheism and Reliance'", "badge": "Insight"}], "80": [{"arabic": "يميته ويحييه وإذا مرض فهو يشفيه وإذا ضعف فهو يقويه وهو الذي يوفقه للطاعة ويرتضيه وهو الذي يطعمه ويسقيه ويحفظه من الهلاك ويحميه ويحرسه بالطعام والشراب عما يهلكه ويرديه ويمكنه من القناعة بقليل القوت ويقربه حتى تضيق به مجاري الشيطان الذي يناويه ويكسر به شهوة النفس التي تعاديه فيدفع شرها ثم يعبد ربه ويتقيه هذا بعد أن يوسع عليه ما يلتذ به ويشتهيه ويكثر عليه ما يهيج بواعثه ويؤكد دواعيه كل ذلك يمتحنه به ويبتليه فينظر كيف يؤثره على ما يهواه وينتحيه وكيف يحفظ أوامره", "english": "And praise belongs to God alone, and blessings upon our master Muḥammad, upon his Family, his Companions, and upon every chosen servant from among the people of the earth and the heavens. And my success is only through God; upon Him I rely and unto Him I turn in repentance.", "book_title": "Harms of the Tongue", "section_title_ar": "Section 638", "section_title_en": "Section 638", "section_index": 638, "anchors": "*(Anchors established)*", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Harms of the Tongue'", "badge": "Insight"}], "88": [{"arabic": "على النار يفتنون يوم لا ينفع مال ولا بنون يوم لا ينفع الظالمين معذرتهم ولهم اللعنة ولهم سوء الدار يوم ترد فيه المعاذير وتبلى السرائر وتظهر الضمائر وتكشف الأستار يوم تخشع فيه الأبصار وتسكن الأصوات ويقل فيه الالتفات وتبرز الخفيات وتظهر الخطيئات يوم يساق العباد ومعهم الأشهاد ويشيب الصغير ويسكر الكبير فيومئذ وضعت الموازين ونشرت الدواوين وبرزت الجحيم وأغلى الحميم وزفرت النار ويئس الكفار وسعرت النيران وتغيرت الألوان وخرس اللسان ونطقت جوارح الإنسان فيا أيها الإنسان ما غرك بربك الكريم حيث أغلق", "english": "So prepare yourself, O wretched one, for this Day of immense magnitude, of prolonged duration, of overwhelming dominion, whose appointed time is near — a Day when you shall see the heaven split asunder, and the stars scattered in its terror, and the shining planets extinguished, and the sun folded up, and the mountains set in motion, and the pregnant camels neglected, and the wild beasts gathered together, and the seas set ablaze, and the souls paired with their bodies, and the Hellfire ignited, and Paradise brought near, and the mountains pulverized, and the earth stretched out — a Day when you shall see the earth shaken with its quaking, and the earth casts forth its burdens. On that Day shall people issue forth in scattered groups to be shown their deeds — a Day when the earth and the mountains are lifted and crushed with a single crushing. Then on that Day the Imminent Event shall come to pass, and the heaven shall split open, for on that Day it shall be frail, and the angels shall be at its edges, and eight shall bear the Throne of your Lord above them on that Day. On that Day you shall be presented — no secret of yours shall remain hidden. A Day when the mountains shall move and you shall see the earth laid bare — a Day when the earth shall be shaken with a violent shaking, and the mountains crumbled to dust, becoming scattered particles — a Day when people shall be like scattered moths, and the mountains like carded wool — a Day when every nursing mother shall forget what she nursed, and every pregnant female shall cast down her burden, and you shall see people drunk, yet they are not drunk, but the chastisement of God is severe — a Day when the earth shall be changed to other than this earth, and the heavens, and they shall appear before God, the One, the All-Compelling — a Day when the mountains shall be blown away as dust, leaving a level, bare plain, wherein you see no crookedness nor curve — a Day when you see the mountains and suppose them solid, yet they pass by like the passing of clouds — a Day when the heaven shall split open and become rosy like molten oil. Then on that Day no human nor jinn shall be asked about his sin. A Day when the disobedient shall be prevented from speech, and shall not be asked about their crimes, but shall be seized by their forelocks and their feet — a Day when every soul shall find what it did of good brought forth present, and what it did of evil, wishing that between it and that evil there were a far distance — a Day when every soul shall know what it has sent ahead, and shall witness what it has forwarded and what it has left behind — a Day when tongues shall be struck mute and the bodily members shall speak — a Day whose mention turned the hair of the Master of the Messengers white, when al-Ṣiddīq (may God be pleased with him) said to him: \"I see that you have turned white-haired, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"Sūrat Hūd and its sisters have made me white-haired\" — namely, al-Wāqiʿah, al-Mursalāt, ʿAmma Yatasāʾalūn, and Idhā al-Shamsu Kuwwirat.", "book_title": "Remembrance of Death and Afterlife", "section_title_ar": "Section 1339", "section_title_en": "The Names and Attributes of the Day of Resurrection — An Exhortation to the Negligent", "section_index": 1339, "anchors": "- Root: يوم (yawm)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"اليوم: وقت طلوع الشمس إلى غروبها، وقد يعبر به عن مدة من الزمان أي مدة كانت\" — the day as a temporal span, extended metaphorically to any epoch or era.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"اليوم يعبر به عن وقت طلوع الشمس إلى غروبها. وقد يعبر به عن مدة من الزمان أي مدة كانت\" — theological usage denotes the appointed time of reckoning, magnified by divine attribution (أيام الله).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): a measured solar period. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"ذكر في أيام العرب كذا أي في وقائعها\" — days as epochal events; thus \"the Day\" is the supreme epochal event of divine justice.\n- Root: نفس (nafs)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: النفس: الروح والذات — the self, soul, or very essence.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النفس: الروح... وقوله: ويحذركم الله نفسه فنفسه: ذاته\" — nafs as the innermost reality of a being; in the eschatological context, souls are \"paired\" (زوجت) with bodies for judgment.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the soul as life-principle. Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه أي دمه\" — nafs as the total self, accountable in its entirety.\n- Root: ارض (arḍ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: الأرض: الجرم المقابل للسماء — the earth as the corporeal substratum beneath the heavens.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الأرض: الجرم المقابل للسماء... ويعبر بها عن أسفل الشيء\" — the earth as the lowest register of creation, subject to total transformation on that Day.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the physical earth. Metaphorical: \"تأرض فلان: لزم الأرض\" — to cling low; on that Day the earth itself is leveled, flattened, and replaced.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The repeated \"يوم\" clauses function as temporal restrictors (ẓurūf) binding each predicate to that single, all-encompassing moment; the accumulation of names (أسامي) serves not as mere repetition but as focused predication upon the multifarious realities of a single event.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Remembrance of Death and Afterlife'", "badge": "Insight"}], "89": [{"arabic": "قلبه لا حال شخصه فمن صفات القلوب تصاغ الصور في الدار الآخرة ولا ينجو إلا من أتى الله بقلب سليم نسأل الله حسن التوفيق بلطفه وكرمه", "english": "The bond linking all these causes is faith (al-īmān) and certainty (al-yaqīn)—by which I mean these very knowledges we have mentioned. The meaning of their being \"certain\" is the absence of doubt and their full dominion over the heart, as has preceded in the exposition of certainty in the Book of Knowledge. And in proportion to one's certainty, the heart becomes humble (yakhsha'). For this reason, ʿĀ'ishah—may God be pleased with her—said: \"The Messenger of God—may God's peace and blessings be upon him—would converse with us and we with him; but when the time of prayer arrived, it was as though he knew us not, nor we him.\" It has also been related that God—Glory be to Him—revealed to Moses—peace be upon him: \"O Moses, when you remember Me, remember Me while your limbs tremble, and be, at the remembrance of Me, humble and tranquil. When you remember Me, place your tongue behind your heart. And when you stand before Me, stand as a lowly servant stands, and call upon Me with a fearful heart and a truthful tongue.\" It was also related that God—Exalted is He—revealed to him: \"Say to the disobedient ones of your community: Let them not remember Me, for I have sworn upon Myself that whoever remembers Me, I will remember him; so if they remember Me, I will remember them with a curse.\" This concerns a disobedient one who is not heedless in his remembrance—how then when heedlessness and disobedience are combined?", "book_title": "Poverty and Abstinence", "section_title_ar": "Section 135", "section_title_en": "Exposition of the Inner Meanings by Which the Life of Prayer is Perfected", "section_index": 135, "anchors": "- Root: خوف (kh-w-f)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core sense of fear, dread, apprehension of harm or punishment.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Fear (al-khawf) is the disturbance of the heart due to anticipation of something detestable; its theological counterpart is hope (al-rajā'), both being states consequent upon knowledge (ma'rifah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqiqah) usage denotes fear of a tangible threat; metaphorical (majaz) usage extends to reverential awe (khashyah) of God's majesty, which is a state of the heart, not a bodily reaction.\n- Root: رجو (r-j-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To hope, expect, desire something good; the opposite of despair (ya's).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Hope (al-rajā') is the heart's tranquil expectation of a beloved matter after its causes have been secured; it is not mere wishful thinking (tamannī) but arises necessarily from certainty in God's promise and knowledge of His bounty.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is anticipation of a favorable outcome; metaphorical usage in theology denotes the soul's reliance on God's grace (karam) as a motivating spiritual state.\n- Root: حيي (ḥ-y-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Life; also shame, modesty (al-ḥayā'), derived from the sense of recoiling from base acts as if by a vital instinct.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Shame (al-ḥayā') is a state of the soul that restrains one from blameworthy acts, arising from the perception of one's own deficiency before the majesty of another; it is a moral faculty, not a mere emotion.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is bashfulness before people; metaphorical usage is the reverential awe before God, born of the awareness of His omniscience over hidden thoughts.\n- Root: خشع (kh-sh-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To be lowly, submissive, humbled; physical stillness and lowering of the gaze.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Khushū' is the heart's humility and stillness before God, manifesting in the body's tranquility; it is the fruit of certainty (yaqīn).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage is bodily stillness; metaphorical usage is the heart's submissiveness, which is the true locus of prayer's life.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of 'Aṭf al-Bayān (Appositional Clarification) — The phrase \"أعني به\" (I mean by it) functions as explanatory apposition, specifying that the preceding term (al-īmān) is identical to the enumerated knowledges (al-ma'ārif), ensuring precise referential identity without ambiguity.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Poverty and Abstinence'", "badge": "Insight"}], "202": [{"arabic": "عليه شيء مما يسرون وما يعلنون وحذرهم أن يأخذهم بغتة وهم لا يشعرون فقال {ما ينظرون إلا صيحة واحدة تأخذهم وهم يخصمون فلا يستطيعون توصية ولا إلى أهلهم يرجعون} والصلاة والسلام على محمد رسوله الذي يسير تحت لوائه النبيون وعلى آله وأصحابه الأئمة المهديين والسادة المرضيين صلاة يوازي عددها عدد ما كان من خلق الله وما سيكون ويحظى ببركتها الأولون والآخرون وسلم تسليما كثيرا أما بعد فإن الغضب شعلة نار اقتبست من نار الله الموقدة التي تطلع على الأفئدة وإنها لمستكنة في طي الفؤاد استكنان الجمر تحت الرماد ويستخرجه الكبر الدفي", "english": "In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. Praise be to God, upon whose pardon and mercy none rely except the hopeful, and from whose evil wrath and assault none fear except the fearful — He who gradually seizes His servants from whence they know not, and who has given dominion over them to their lusts, commanding them to abandon what they desire, and who has tried them with anger while charging them to swallow their rage in what provokes them. Then He surrounded them with hardships and pleasures, and granted them respite to see how they would act. He tested their love through them, to make known the truth of what they claim. He made known to them that nothing is hidden from Him of what they conceal or proclaim, and warned them lest He seize them suddenly while they are unaware. For He said: {«They await but a single blast which will seize them while they are disputing; so they will not be able to make a bequest, nor to their families will they return»} (Q. 36:49-50). And prayers and peace be upon Muhammad, His Messenger, beneath whose banner the prophets walk, and upon his family and companions — the rightly-guided imams and the pleasing masters — prayers whose number equals the number of what has been of God's creation and what will be, and by whose blessing the first and the last are favored — and abundant peace.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Envy", "section_title_ar": "Section 700", "section_title_en": "The Book of Condemnation of Anger, Spite, and Envy — Book Five of the Quarter of Destroyers from The Revival of the Religious Sciences", "section_index": 700, "anchors": "- Root: غضب (ghadab)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of anger, rage, fury; the boiling and agitation of the blood\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — when attributed to God, it means retribution (intiqām) alone, not emotional agitation; the Prophet described it as \"a live coal kindled in the heart of the son of Adam\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — literal anger is the boiling of the blood in living beings; metaphorical usage extends to inanimate things like fire and the reins of a mount\n- Root: قلب (qalb)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The heart; also the turning, overturning, and transformation of a thing from one state to another\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — the heart is so named for its constant turning (taqallub) and fluctuation between states; it is the seat of understanding and the locus of divine address\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — literal is the physical organ; metaphorical is the subtle spiritual reality (laṭīfah rabbāniyyah) that is the locus of knowledge and will\n- Root: حسد (hasad)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Envy; the wishing for removal of another's blessing\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — envy is the desire for the removal of a blessing from one who deserves it, sometimes accompanied by striving to remove it; the believer envies (ghibṭah) while the hypocrite envies (hasad)\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — \"Envy consumes the body as fire consumes wood\"; the envier is one who wishes evil upon the blessed\n- Root: هلك (halak)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Perdition, destruction, ruin; death\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance — three senses: (1) loss of a thing from one's possession while it exists elsewhere, (2) corruption and dissolution of a thing, (3) death; the Quran uses it for all three\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal vs Metaphorical — literal is physical destruction; metaphorical is the ruin of one's religion and afterlife through spiritual corruption\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The permissibility of interposing elements between a preposition and its object when the intervening material constitutes a complete, meaningful unit, as in the Quranic pattern of extended periodic sentences that delay resolution for rhetorical effect.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Condemnation of Envy'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "212": [{"arabic": "يبصرون ولا يسمعون لأنهم عن السمع معزولون وعن آيات ربهم محجوبون {يعلمون ظاهرا من الحياة الدنيا وهم عن الآخرة هم غافلون} وما أريد بالسمع السمع الظاهر فإن الذينأريدوا به ما كانوا معزولين عنه وإنما أريد به السمع الباطن ولا يدرك بالسمع الظاهر إلا الأصوات ويشارك الإنسان فيه سائر الحيوانات فأما السمع الباطن فيدرك به لسان الحال الذي هو نطق وراء نطق المقال يشبه قول القائل حكاية لكلام الوتد والحائط قال الجدار للوتد لم تشقني فقال سل من يدقنى ولم يتركني ورائي الحجر الذي ورائي وما من ذرة في السماوات و", "english": "I say: As for the signs of God in His earth, in contemplating them there are benefits for the discerning seeker of insight. For in them are contiguous tracts, and in them are mountains, wildernesses, seas, and varieties of animals and plants. And there is not a single thing among them but that it bears witness to God of His Oneness and glorifies Him with an eloquent tongue (lisān dhalq) that none perceives save him who gives ear while being present as a witness {«وَأَلْقَى السَّمْعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيدٌ»} (And gives ear while he is a witness) [Q. 50:37].", "book_title": "Etiquette of Travel", "section_title_ar": "Section 466", "section_title_en": "The Book of Seclusion — The Benefits of Association and Travel: Association with Increased Occupation and Endurance of Hardships", "section_index": 466, "anchors": "- Root: سمع (s-m-')\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The faculty of hearing in the ear; also used for the ear itself, and metaphorically for understanding or obedience.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"السمع\" denotes both the physical faculty and, in theological contexts, the inner hearing of the heart by which divine truths are apprehended — distinct from mere auditory perception.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): hearing sounds. Metaphorical (Majaz): \"سمع الله لمن حمده\" (God hears him who praises Him) means acceptance and response; \"ألقى السمع\" (gave ear) implies attentive presence of heart.\n- Root: سفر (s-f-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To uncover, reveal, or travel; the traveler (musāfir) is one who uncovers new horizons.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"السفر: كشف الغطاء\" — uncovering the veil; journeying as a means of unveiling hidden realities.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical travel. Metaphorical: \"وجه مسفر\" (a face radiant with joy); the inner journey from the narrow confines of outward perception to the expanse of inner vision.\n- Root: ظهر (ẓ-h-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The back; outward or visible aspect.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Used metaphorically for the outward, apparent dimension of things, as opposed to the inner (bāṭin).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the back of a beast. Metaphorical: \"قلبت الأمر ظهرا لبطن\" (turned the matter over, back and belly) — examining all aspects; the visible world (ʿālam al-shahādah) as the outward face of reality.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Used to distinguish the exclusive nature of inner hearing (al-samʿ al-bāṭin) as the sole means of apprehending the language of states (lisān al-ḥāl), in contrast to outward hearing shared with beasts.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Etiquette of Travel'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "213": [{"arabic": "الله ولقوله ولا تجعلوا مع الله إلها آخر فمن لم يره في كل شيء فقد رأى غيره وكل ما التفت إليه العبد سوى الله تعالى تضمن التفاته شيئا من الشرك الخفي بل التوحيد الخالص أن لا يرى في كل شيء إلا الله عز وجل العاشر التبري وأعني به أن يتبرأ من حوله وقوته والالتفات إلى نفسه بين الرضا والتزكية فإذا تلا بآيات الوعد والمدح للصالحين فلا يشهد نفسه عند ذلك بل يشهد الموقنين والصديقين فيها ويتشوف إلى أن يلحقه الله عز وجل بهم وإذا تلا آيات المقت وذم العصاة والمقصرين شهد على نفسه هناك وقدر أنه المخا", "english": "For this reason, Yūsuf ibn Asbāṭ said: \"I intend to recite the Qur'an, but when I recall what is in it, I fear abhorrence (al-maqt), so I turn instead to glorification (al-tasbīḥ) and seeking forgiveness (al-istighfār).\"", "book_title": "Condemnation of Pride and Conceit", "section_title_ar": "Section 231", "section_title_en": "** The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section 231: On the Inward Conditions of Qur'anic Recitation (Continued)", "section_index": 231, "anchors": "**\n- Root: وجل (w-j-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — the stirring of fear/apprehension within\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف. يقال: وجل يوجل وجلا، فهو وجل. قال تعالى: {إنما المؤمنون الذين إذا ذكر الله وجلت قلوبهم}\" — the theological state of the heart's trembling upon remembrance of God\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال، وقد وجل وجلا\" — the physical/emotional state of fear. Metaphorical (Majaz): The heart's trembling as the seat of spiritual perception\n- Root: قلب (q-l-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — turning and transforming\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه، كقلب الثوب، وقلب الإنسان\" — the heart as that which is constantly turning/transforming between states\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" — physical turning. Metaphorical: \"قلب المعلم الصبيان: صرفهم إلى بيوتهم\" — the heart's turning toward or away from spiritual realities\n- Root: نفس (n-f-s)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, soul, spirit — that which is breathed\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النفس: الروح\" — the soul as the animating principle; also the self as the locus of blameworthy attributes\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"شيء نفيس ومنفس\" — preciousness. Metaphorical: \"دفق نفسه أي دمه\" — the self as that which must be transcended in spiritual realization\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد (Restriction & Focused Predication) — governing the precise delimitation of spiritual states (أحوال) and their hierarchical gradation (درجات)\n\n---\n\n#", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Condemnation of Pride and Conceit'", "badge": "Insight"}], "215": [{"arabic": "فالعلم من أعظم ما يتكبر به ولذلك قال تعالى لنبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم واخفض جناحك لمن اتبعك من المؤمنين وقال عز وجل ولو كنت فظا غليظ القلب لانفضوا من حولك ووصف أولياءه فقال أذلة على المؤمنين أعزة على الكافرين وكذلك قال صلى الله عليه وسلم فيما رواه العباس رضي الله عنه يكون قوم يقرءون القرآن لا يجاوز حناجرهم يقولون قد قرأنا القرآن فمن أقرأ منا ومن أعلم منا ثم التفت إلى أصحابه وقال أولئك منكم أيها الأمة أولئك هم", "english": "The second aspect by which the vice of pride is magnified is that it calls to opposing Allah the Exalted in His commands. For the arrogant man, when he hears the truth from a servant among the servants of Allah, disdains to accept it and girds himself for its denial. For this reason you see the disputants in matters of religion claiming that they are investigating the secrets of the religion, yet they engage in mutual denial—the denial of the arrogant. Whenever the truth becomes clear upon the tongue of one of them, the other refuses to accept it out of pride, girds himself for its denial, and resorts to every stratagem to repel it by whatever obfuscation he can muster. This is among the moral traits of the disbelievers and the hypocrites, for Allah the Exalted described them, saying: {«وَقَالَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَا تَسْمَعُوا لِهَذَا الْقُرْآنِ وَالْغَوْا فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَغْلِبُونَ»} (And those who disbelieve said: \"Do not listen to this Quran and make noise therein, perhaps you may prevail.\") So whoever disputes for the sake of victory and silencing the opponent—not to seize the truth when it appears to him—has shared with them in this moral trait. Likewise, this pride drives one to refuse admonition, as Allah the Exalted said: {«وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُ اتَّقِ اللَّهَ أَخَذَتْهُ الْعِزَّةُ بِالْإِثْمِ»} (And when it is said to him, \"Fear Allah,\" pride in sin seizes him.) It is narrated that ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, recited this verse and then said: {«إِنَّا لِلَّهِ وَإِنَّا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعُونَ»} (Indeed, we belong to Allah and to Him we return.) A man rose to enjoin good and was killed; then another rose and said: \"They kill those who enjoin justice among the people\"—and the arrogant one who opposed him and the one who commanded him was killed out of pride.", "book_title": "Condemnation of Pride and Conceit", "section_title_ar": "Section 857", "section_title_en": "The Second Aspect by Which the Vice of Pride (Kibr) Is Magnified: That It Leads to Opposing Allah in His Commands", "section_index": 857, "anchors": "- Root: كبر (K-B-R)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of bigness, magnitude, and seniority; al-kibr is the internal disposition of self-magnification.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Kabīr and al-Ṣaghīr are relative terms (mutadāyifān); kibr as a moral vice is the soul's claim to a station above its due, entailing disdain for others.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) usage concerns physical or quantitative magnitude; metaphorical (majāz) usage here denotes arrogance and haughtiness—\"كبر عليه\" (he disdained it).\n- Root: علم (ʿ-L-M)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Knowing a thing's reality; the root also carries the sense of a mark/trace (ʿalam) by which one is guided.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): True knowledge (ʿilm) is apprehension of a thing's essence or judgment about it; the highest form is knowledge of Allah, the self, and the Final End—this engenders fear (khashyah).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: perception and awareness; metaphorical: the \"marks\" (maʿālim) of religion—the distinguishing signs of guidance.\n- Root: نفس (N-F-S)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The self, soul, or spirit; that which is valued and precious.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-Nafs denotes the soul or self; in theological usage it may refer to the essence (dhāt) of a thing.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the soul; metaphorical: self-worth and self-regard—the arrogant man \"magnifies his own soul\" (istaʿẓama nafsahu).\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The verse {إِنَّمَا يَخْشَى اللَّهَ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْعُلَمَاءُ} restricts true fear of Allah exclusively to the learned, delimiting the predicate to the subject.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Condemnation of Pride and Conceit'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "216": [{"arabic": "بالمعصية ولذلك قال الله تعالى لنبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم في عشيرته {فإن عصوك فقل إني بريء مما تعملون} ولم يقل إني بريء منكم مراعاة لحق القرابة ولحمة النسب وإلى هذا أشار أبو الدرداء لما قيل له ألا تبغض أخاك وقد فعل كذا فقال إنما أبغض عمله وإلا فهو أخي وأخوة الدين أوكد من أخوة القرابة ولذلك قيل لحكيم أيما احب إليك أخوك أو صديقك فقال إنما أحب أخي إذا كان صديقا لي وكان الحسن يقول كم من أخ لم تلده أمك ولذلك قيل", "english": "Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) held the view of severance, saying: \"When your brother turns away from what he once was, then hate him from the very perspective from which you loved him.\" He considered this to be a requirement of loving for Allah's sake and hating for Allah's sake.", "book_title": "Duties of Brotherhood", "section_title_ar": "Section 424", "section_title_en": "On the Error of a Friend: Between Severance and Gentleness in Brotherhood", "section_index": 424, "anchors": "- Root: لطف (luṭf)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Gentleness, subtlety, refinement; the opposite of harshness and coarseness.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The subtle divine reality (laṭīfah) that perceives the finest nuances of affairs; also gentleness (rifq) in dealing.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: that which is not coarse. Metaphorical: \"I was gentle with him\" (laṭaftu bihi) — showing affection and gentleness in dealing, and \"he is gentle with this matter\" — skillful in managing it.\n- Root: دين (dīn)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Religion, creed, judgment, recompense; the comprehensive term for one's obligatory practices and beliefs.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The root denotes indebtedness and obedience; the religion (dīn) is that by which one is bound to the Divine command.\n- Root: عقد (ʿaqd)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To tie, bind, contract; the knot of brotherhood (ʿaqd al-ukhuwwah) as a binding covenant.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): A firm resolution or covenant that obligates its fulfillment.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — Used to distinguish the precise scope of a ruling, e.g., \"I only hate his deed\" (innamā ubghiḍu ʿamalahu), restricting hatred to the act, not the person.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Duties of Brotherhood'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "218": [{"arabic": "أنه متكلف متواجد فعرفه أن الذي يراه حين يقوم هو الخصم في قيامه لغير الله تعالى ولو كان الرجل صادقا لما جلس فإذا قد رجع حاصل الوجد إلى مكاشفات وإلى حالات واعلم أن كل واحد منهما ينقسم إلى ما يمكن التعبير عنه عند الافاقة منه وإلى ما لا تمكن العبارة عنه أصلا ولعلك تستبعد حالة أو علما لا تعلم حقيقته ولا يمكن التعبير عنه عن حقيقته فلا تستبعد ذلك فإنك تجد في أحوالك القريبة لذلك شواهد أما العلم فكم من فقيه تعرض عليه مسألتان متشابهتان في الصورة ويدرك الفقيه بذوقه أن بينهما فرقا في الحكم", "english": "So Dhu al-Nun fell upon his face. Then another man stood up, and Dhu al-Nun said: \"He who sees you when you stand up.\" So that man sat down. And this was an unveiling (iṭṭilāʿ) by Dhu al-Nun upon that man's heart—that he was affected (mutakallif) and feigning ecstasy (mutawājid). Thus he made known to him that the One who sees him when he stands is the adversary (khaṣm) in his standing for other than God—may He be exalted. And had the man been truthful, he would not have sat down.", "book_title": "Audition and Ecstasy", "section_title_ar": "Section 510", "section_title_en": "The Reality of Ecstasy (Wajd): Its Divisions into Unveilings and States, and What Can and Cannot Be Expressed", "section_index": 510, "anchors": "- Root: وجد (w-j-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of finding, attaining, and passionate emotion; al-wajd is the intense state of the heart's finding.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological terms, al-wajd denotes the heart's direct apprehension of spiritual realities—an experiential knowledge distinct from discursive reasoning.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (haqiqah) usage refers to finding something lost; metaphorical (majaz) usage refers to the soul's emotional states of ecstasy and yearning that overwhelm the rational faculty.\n- Root: ذوق (dh-w-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Literally \"tasting\"; the direct sensory perception by the palate.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Metaphorically, the soul's immediate, non-discursive apprehension of truths—a direct \"taste\" that bypasses conceptual mediation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): The metaphorical transfer (naql) from physical tasting to intellectual and spiritual perception; that which is known by direct experience cannot be conveyed to one who lacks the experience.\n- Root: شوق (sh-w-q)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Intense longing and yearning that stirs the soul toward its beloved.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The innate inclination (mayl) of the soul toward its origin; in the human constitution, a vestige of the primordial covenant with the higher world.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal usage for the yearning of a lover; metaphorical usage for the soul's unconscious longing for the celestial realm (al-ʿālam al-aʿlā) of which it has only heard names and attributes.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Specification (al-ḥaṣr wa al-taqyīd)—the use of conditional and exceptive constructions (in/ law/ illā) to delineate the precise boundaries of what can and cannot be expressed, and to distinguish genuine states from affected ones.", "content_type": "spiritual", "topic": "Al-Ghazali's epistemic insights into the spiritual heart and inner faith, from 'Audition and Ecstasy'", "badge": "Insight"}, {"arabic": "وقال عكرمة في قوله عز وجل الذي يراك حين تقوم وتقلبك في الساجدين قال قيامه وركوعه وسجوده وجلوسه وأما الركوع والسجود فينبغي أن تجدد عندهما ذكر كبرياء الله سبحانه وترفع يديك مستجيرا بعفو الله عز وجل من عقابه بتجديد نية ومتبعا سنة نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم ثم تستأنف له ذلا وتواضعا بركوعك وتجتهد في ترقيق قلبك وتجديد خشوعك وتستشعر ذلك وعز مولاك واتضاعك وعلو ربك وتستعين على تقرير ذلك في قلبك بلسانك فتسبح ربك وتشهد له بالعظمة وأنه أعظم من كل عظيم وتكرر ذلك على قلبك لتؤكده بالتكرار ثم ترتفع من ركوعك راجيا أنه راحم", "english": "For this reason, he, peace be upon him, said: \"Give us rest, O Bilāl\" (1) — meaning, give us rest through it (the prayer) and through the call to it, for his delight, peace be upon him, was in it.", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "section_title_ar": "Section 138", "section_title_en": "The Inner Works of Prayer: Unveiling the Heart's Secrets in the Ritual Prayer (Asrār al-Ṣalāh)", "section_index": 138, "anchors": "- Root: قلب (Q-L-B)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To turn a thing over, to revolve it, to divert it from one state to another; the heart as that which is constantly turning and fluctuating.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"قلب الشيء: تصريفه وصرفه عن وجه إلى وجه\" — The heart is that which is turned and diverted; its rectitude lies in its orientation towards God, its ruin in its turning towards other than Him.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): \"قلب الشيء قلبا: حوله عن وجهه\" (to turn a thing from its face). Metaphorical (Majaz): \"قلب المعلم الصبيان: صرفهم إلى بيوتهم\" (the teacher turned the boys towards their homes) — thus the heart's turning is its direction and intent.\n- Root: وجه (W-J-H)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: The face; the foremost, noblest, and most apparent part of a thing.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"ولما كان الوجه أول ما يستقبلك، وأشرف ما في ظاهر البدن استعمل في مستقبل كل شيء، وفي أشرفه ومبدئه\" — The face is used metaphorically for the essence and the direction of a thing; the \"face of the heart\" is its intention and aspiration.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"واجهته مواجهة ووجاها\" (to face one another). Metaphorical: \"هذا وجه الثوب. ووجه القوم، وهؤلاء وجوه البلد\" (the face of a garment, the chiefs of a people) — thus the \"face\" of the heart is its foremost orientation.\n- Root: وجل (W-J-L)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: A trembling of the heart from fear or awe.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجل: استشعار الخوف\" — The sensing of fear; the heart's tremor before the majesty of the Divine.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"رجل وجل، وقوم وجال، وقد وجل وجلا\" — A man trembling with fear.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The particle \"innamā\" restricts and confines the predicate to the subject alone, negating it from all else. This is crucial for understanding \"إنما هذه الظواهر تحريكات للبواطن\" — the outward acts are *only* movements to stir the inward realities, nothing more.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Ethics"}], "224": [{"arabic": "قال الله تعالى {والشعراء يتبعهم الغاوون ألم تر أنهم في كل واد يهيمون} وقال تعالى {وما علمناه الشعر وما ينبغي له} وأكثر ما اعتاده الوعاظ من الأشعار ما يتعلق بالتواصف في العشق وجمال المعشوق وروح الوصال وألم الفراق والمجلس لا يحوي إلا أجلاف العوام وبواطنهم مشحونة بالشهوات وقلوبهم غير منفكة عن الالتفات إلى الصور المليحة فلا تحرك الأشعار من قلوبهم إلا ما هو مستكن فيها فتشتعل فيها نيران الشهوات فيزعقون ويتواجدون وأكثر ذلك أو كله يرجع إلى نوع فساد فلا ينبغي أن يستعمل من الشعر إلا ما فيه موعظة أو حكمة على سب", "english": "Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may God be pleased with him, said to his son ʿUmar — having heard him composing sajʿ — \"This is what makes me dislike you. I will never fulfill your need until you repent.\" This was said when his son had come to him seeking a favor. And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rawāḥah when he spoke in sajʿ of three words: \"Beware of sajʿ, O Ibn Rawāḥah.\" Thus, the forbidden sajʿ is the artificially contrived kind that exceeds two words. For this reason, when a man spoke concerning the blood-money for a fetus — saying, \"How shall we pay blood-money for one who neither drank, nor ate, nor cried out, nor wailed? Such a one's blood is void\" — the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, replied: \"Sajʿ like the sajʿ of the bedouins!\"", "book_title": "Book of Knowledge", "section_title_ar": "Section 31", "section_title_en": "On the Etiquette of Preaching: The Condemnation of Artificial Sajʿ, Excessive Poetry, and the Perils of Shataḥ and Taʿwīl", "section_index": 31, "anchors": "- Root: سجع (sajʿa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Rhymed prose; from the root meaning \"to coo\" (as a dove), indicating a measured, melodious cadence in speech.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological discourse, sajʿ is permissible when natural but blameworthy when artificially cultivated (takalluf), as it shifts focus from meaning to ornamentation.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) — natural rhythmic speech; Metaphorical (majāz) — the \"sajʿ of the bedouins\" (sajʿ al-aʿrāb) as a pejorative for empty, affected eloquence.\n- Root: شعر (shiʿr)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Poetry; from the root denoting perception and fine discernment (shuʿūr), as the poet grasps subtle meanings.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Poetry is blameworthy when it stirs base appetites, but praiseworthy when it conveys wisdom (ḥikmah), as in the prophetic saying \"Indeed from poetry there is wisdom.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — metered, rhymed speech; Metaphorical — the \"poetry\" of the heart's inclination, where listeners project their own passions onto what they hear.\n- Root: شطح (shaṭaḥa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To overflow, to gush forth; originally of a water-skin bursting, then applied to ecstatic utterances that overflow the bounds of conventional discourse.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In Sufi terminology, shataḥ refers to utterances arising from overwhelming spiritual states (ḥāl) that, when voiced to the unworthy, cause corruption.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — physical overflowing; Metaphorical — the soul's overflow in speech that exceeds the speaker's intentional control.\n- Root: أول (taʿwīl)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To return something to its origin or end; interpretation that traces a word back to its intended meaning.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Taʿwīl is legitimate only when supported by textual (naqlī) or rational (ʿaqlī) evidence; arbitrary taʿwīl that severs words from their established senses destroys religious trust.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal — the apparent sense (ẓāhir); Metaphorical — the inner sense (bāṭin), which is only valid when the literal sense is impossible or when transmitted authority sanctions it.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Bāb al-Ḥaṣr wa al-Taqyīd bi-innamā (Restriction and Focused Predication) — The text repeatedly uses restrictive constructions (innamā, laysa...illā) to delimit permissible preaching, poetry, and interpretation, distinguishing the praiseworthy from the blameworthy with syntactic precision.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Book of Knowledge'", "badge": "Hadith"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 10, 7850]], "26:1": [[1, 10, 7850]], "2": [[1, 320, 838], [2, 838, 2113], [3, 2113, 3003], [4, 3003, 4170]], "26:2": [[1, 320, 838], [2, 838, 2113], [3, 2113, 3003], [4, 3003, 4170]], "3": [[1, 200, 1083], [2, 1083, 1825], [3, 1